-limits obstruction and finite model; direct RH progress not established.", "difficulty": "Elementary two-root case; substantial general uniform finite-cluster analysis; very high arithmetic transfer.", "provenance_file": "connections/equivalence_track.jsonl", "checkpoint_verification": "independently checked scoped claim; director_adjudication.md", "next_step_checkpoint": "Two-root uniform remainder now proved in THM-E010; next fixed-multi-cluster uniform bounds and grouped arithmetic residues."}','A separation-independent passage from fixed-distinct zero jets to an infinite-zero approximation requires clusterwise estimates; the polynomial 1/N separation model has a different leading constant from the fixed-distinct-root limit.','connections/equivalence_track.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-F001','connections/connections.jsonl',43,'independent reconstructions complete; director adjudication accepted at scoped conditional-reconstruction level','connections/formal_round2.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-F001", "source_theorems": ["PAPER-A005:Lemma2.5", "PAPER-A005:Proposition3.3", "THM-F003"], "kind": "finite transfer strengthening under additional checked prefix conditions", "statement": "For the pinned first-window data, absorb telescoping prefix potentials into pressure not charged at chain endpoints: alpha*S+Phi_left-Phi_right<=6alpha*spread-30alpha*theta. Replace source boundary6y+Omega=.432480 by6y-30alpha theta=.2580135.", "compatible_assumptions": "Same7point local inequality, nonnegative pair weights and offset budgets, theta-separated real chain, frozen source prefixes satisfy390 exact PL knot checks and30 theta endpoints, y>=6alpha theta; original e nonnegative symmetric assumptions suffice.", "already_proved": "Source local certificate components independently reconstructed; advocate and skeptic derive boundary identity and finite conditions. Director adjudication pending.", "conjectural": "Publication novelty and usefulness after all finite-T analytic errors are made explicit; no asymptotic zero-proportion gain.", "next_step": "Independently adjudicate the finite proof, formalize real interpolation/transfer, then derive explicit trace/smoothing errors to assess finite-height impact.", "potential_counterexamples": "Dropping y>=6alpha theta is invalid even when C>0: theta1,alpha1/100,y11/200,all weights/potentials0,per-position rewards11/1400 satisfy local7point inequality but singleton would require0>=1/40.", "tests": "839_boundary_advocate.py; independent transfer skeptic code; Std-only finite Lean certificate covers data inequalities, not real transfer.", "significance": "Concrete bounded-loss improvement and reusable boundary bookkeeping; no RH advance claimed.", "difficulty": "Elementary finite proof, substantially harder explicit analytic application", "verification_status": "independent reconstructions complete; director adjudication accepted at scoped conditional-reconstruction level", "director_adjudication": "Accepted at the explicit scoped conditional-reconstruction level; audits/adversarial_reviews/director_round3_adjudication.md", "id": "CONN-F001", "provenance_file": "connections/formal_round2.jsonl"}','For the pinned first-window data, absorb telescoping prefix potentials into pressure not charged at chain endpoints: alpha*S+Phi_left-Phi_right<=6alpha*spread-30alpha*theta. Replace source boundary6y+Omega=.432480 by6y-30alpha theta=.2580135.','connections/formal_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-F002','connections/connections.jsonl',44,'conditional connection independently reconstructed; director adjudication accepted at scoped conditional-reconstruction level','proposals/independent_campaigns/zero_buffer_localization_round2.md; audits/adversarial_reviews/AF_zero_buffer_VK_skeptic_round2.md','{"connection_id": "CONN-F002", "source_theorems": ["PAPER-A006:Section2-p6-Korobov-Vinogradov-strip", "PAPER-A004:Lemma2.1-eq2.8", "PAPER-A004:Theorem5.7-prime-moment", "THM-F007"], "proposed_claim": "THM-F008: a classical zero-free strip yields arbitrarily logarithmic savings in the unbuffered discarded matrix, allowing the existing HS moment transfer without growing a zero buffer.", "compatible_assumptions": "Classical zeta only; FE gives both beta edges at comparable heights; fixed bounded C2 window with uniform decay; far heights use global multiplicity counts. No growing conductor claim.", "already_proved": "Independent conditional localization/norm arguments; the zero-free theorem is classical and explicitly stated in inspected BGSTB source, its original proof not audited.", "conjectural_or_pending": "Novelty check remains; director accepted the explicit scoped conditional result; full prime-side moment not independently established here.", "next_precise_step": "Formalize an abstract bounded-strip sampling/nuclear localization lemma and the relative-HS transfer, with explicit dependencies on the strip and window norms.", "counterexamples_or_barriers": "Sharp unsmoothed Fourier tails do not satisfy the C2 decay premise; operator norm need not tend to0, so applications requiring Weyl cannot silently use this weaker norm conclusion.", "tests": "Analytic proof, no numerical agreement used as proof.", "significance": "Proof simplification and a reusable truncation lemma; no improvement to asymptotic zero proportions.", "difficulty": "Elementary Fourier/localization estimates once source hypotheses are isolated; formalization and quantitative constants remain.", "status": "conditional connection independently reconstructed; director adjudication accepted at scoped conditional-reconstruction level", "evidence": "proposals/independent_campaigns/zero_buffer_localization_round2.md; audits/adversarial_reviews/AF_zero_buffer_VK_skeptic_round2.md", "director_adjudication": "Accepted at the explicit scoped conditional-reconstruction level; audits/adversarial_reviews/director_round3_adjudication.md", "explicit_scope_countermodel": "audits/adversarial_reviews/AF_no_buffer_operator_countermodel.md: one fixed synthetic multiset satisfies strip/symmetry/RvM/local-count hypotheses but its unbuffered operator tail diverges; no actual-zeta/explicit-formula claim; director accepted this explicit scoped countermodel.", "original_source_theorems": ["PAPER-A006§2p6 Vinogradov-Korobov strip as external input", "PAPER-A004 Lemma2.1/eq2.8 and Theorem5.7 prime-side part", "THM-F007"], "source_reference_locators": {"PAPER-A006:Section2-p6-Korobov-Vinogradov-strip": "Baluyot–Goldston–Suriajaya–Turnage-Butterbaugh, arXiv:2306.04799v1, §2 p. 6 first paragraph; for the zero-free majorant see p. 4, eqs. (2.9)–(2.11). The strip enters as a classical external result.", "PAPER-A004:Lemma2.1-eq2.8": "Alpöge–Furman, arXiv:2608.13637v2, §2 pp. 4–5, eq. (2.8) and Lemma 2.1 (the Poisson–Gabor identity).", "PAPER-A004:Theorem5.7-prime-moment": "Alpöge–Furman, arXiv:2608.13637v2, §5 p. 11, Theorem 5.7, prime-side second-moment component."}, "id": "CONN-F002", "provenance_file": "connections/formal_round2.jsonl"}','THM-F008: a classical zero-free strip yields arbitrarily logarithmic savings in the unbuffered discarded matrix, allowing the existing HS moment transfer without growing a zero buffer.','connections/formal_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-F003','connections/connections.jsonl',45,'Accepted scoped negative control; not a result about actual zeta zeros.','audits/adversarial_reviews/AF_no_buffer_operator_countermodel.md','{"connection_id": "CONN-F003", "source_theorems": ["THM-F007", "THM-F008", "THM-F010", "PAPER-A004:Lemma3.4", "PAPER-A004:Section6"], "mathematically_explicit_connection": "The relativeHS truncation sufficient for the section6 rank-trace argument cannot be substituted into Weyl arguments requiring operatorerroro(1). The same abstract geometric/strip/count hypotheses admit THM-F010, whose diagonal diverges on a fixed multiset while its relativeHS error vanishes.", "compatible_assumptions": "Same smooth fixed cutoff and critical sampling; synthetic multiset meets bounded strip, symmetries, local counts and RvM main term.", "already_proved": "Explicit fixed-multiset countermodel and analytic Fourier endpoint asymptotic, independently reconstructed and director-reviewed.", "conjectural_or_pending": "Actual zeta operator-tail behavior and any further implications of the full prime-side moment are outside this construction; no novelty claim.", "next_precise_step": "For any proposed operator-based extension, state and prove the additional hypothesis that rules out the sparse off-line quartet obstruction, rather than importing relativeHS control as operator control.", "counterexamples_or_barriers": "THM-F010 itself; it does not satisfy a proved zeta explicit formula or asserted prime-side asymptotic.", "tests": "Ordinary analytic proof, with explicit positive J(-eta); no floating-point argument.", "significance": "Precise scope barrier for transferring an accepted truncation simplification to stronger spectral claims.", "difficulty": "Elementary but quantifier-sensitive; one fixed infinite multiset avoids a merely nonuniform-family example.", "status": "Accepted scoped negative control; not a result about actual zeta zeros.", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/AF_no_buffer_operator_countermodel.md", "original_source_theorems": ["THM-F007", "THM-F008", "THM-F010", "PAPER-A004 Lemma3.4 and section6"], "source_reference_locators": {"PAPER-A004:Lemma3.4": "Alpöge–Furman, arXiv:2608.13637v2, §3 p. 6, Lemma 3.4 (Weyl).", "PAPER-A004:Section6": "Alpöge–Furman, arXiv:2608.13637v2, §6 pp. 11–12, the rank, trace and second-moment argument."}, "id": "CONN-F003", "provenance_file": "connections/formal_round2.jsonl"}','The relativeHS truncation sufficient for the section6 rank-trace argument cannot be substituted into Weyl arguments requiring operatorerroro(1). The same abstract geometric/strip/count hypotheses admit THM-F010, whose diagonal diverges on a fixed multiset while its relativeHS error vanishes.','connections/formal_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-F004','connections/connections.jsonl',46,'Accepted scoped correction/qualification, no main-theorem error claim.','audits/adversarial_reviews/christoffel_scope_proposer_round3.md','{"connection_id": "CONN-F004", "source_theorems": ["THM-F011", "THM-F012", "PAPER-A004:Section7.2(d)", "PAPER-A004:Section7.2(f)"], "mathematically_explicit_connection": "Replace an unrestricted ordinary-Christoffel atom bound by a polynomial majorant of the negative halfline. This corrects the generic inference while preserving the source-specific four-moment certificate and its conditional13/18 simple-critical consequence.", "compatible_assumptions": "Finite Hermitian matrices, normalized real trace moments, d>=1; source-specific number-theoretic conclusion additionally requires HL*(4), d/N->1 and the stated simple/multiple/off-pair count bounds.", "already_proved": "The finite moment inequality, explicit66-dimensional counterexample and particular polynomial arithmetic, independently reconstructed and director-accepted.", "conjectural_or_pending": "The higher prime-side moment hypothesis is not established. Sharp optimality of general one-sided moment programs needs its own hypotheses.", "next_precise_step": "For each higher-moment proposal export an explicit q>=1_{(-infinity,0]} certificate and its exact moment objective; do not equate an atom Christoffel minimum with a halfline optimum without checking.", "counterexamples_or_barriers": "THM-F011 has a positive-definite moment matrix and the same m1,m2 as the source, but its minimizing square fails on a negative eigenvalue. Full zeta constraints are not modeled.", "tests": "Exact Fraction orthogonality and polynomial objective check; independent different witness and director review.", "significance": "Prevents an overgeneralized moment inference and gives a concrete valid conditional certificate. No improved unconditional density.", "status": "Accepted scoped correction/qualification, no main-theorem error claim.", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/christoffel_scope_proposer_round3.md", "original_source_theorems": ["THM-F011", "THM-F012", "PAPER-A004§7.2(d),(f)"], "source_reference_locators": {"PAPER-A004:Section7.2(d)": "Alpöge–Furman, arXiv:2608.13637v2, §7.2(d) p. 13, the informal ordinary Christoffel-function inference.", "PAPER-A004:Section7.2(f)": "Alpöge–Furman, arXiv:2608.13637v2, §7.2(f) p. 13, the conditional sine-Gram moment route and its four-moment specialization."}, "id": "CONN-F004", "provenance_file": "connections/formal_round2.jsonl"}','Replace an unrestricted ordinary-Christoffel atom bound by a polynomial majorant of the negative halfline. This corrects the generic inference while preserving the source-specific four-moment certificate and its conditional13/18 simple-critical consequence.','connections/formal_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-G001','connections/connections.jsonl',47,'Explicit proof plus independent parent check; no external novelty review.','connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-G001", "source_theorems": ["THM-G003", "THM-G010", "THM-G011"], "kind": "explicit hypothesis-deletion obstruction", "statement": "Positive Euler exponents, reciprocal functional equation, rational local polynomials and alternating self-duality do not supply the geometric-monodromy pole control required by DeligneI(3.2). The explicit A=[[2,1],[1,3]] yields both a formal positive zeta with off-circle roots and a genuine constant-arithmetic lisse-sheaf test.", "compatible_assumptions": "Formal zeta satisfies the listed rationality/positivity/symmetry axioms. For ℓ≠5 the sheaf has geometric Frobenius A, pairing to Qℓ(−1), and rational local determinants. Its geometric monodromy is trivial, so the open-Sp hypothesis is expressly NOT satisfied.", "new_claim_suggested": "Use this construction as a reusable mandatory negative control for proposals that infer purity from the weaker axioms. No literature novelty is asserted.", "already_proved": "All-degree nonnegative Euler exponents by primitive-orbit injection; alternating multiplier5; continuous lisse-sheaf realization and explicit tensor L-function poles.", "conjectural": "Whether any particular number-field proposal has stronger axioms sufficient to evade this obstruction remains unassessed.", "next_step": "Review the all-degree proof independently and test candidate trace/spectral models against precisely the same list of axioms.", "potential_counterexamples": "A model with actual geometric open-Sp monodromy or a positive invariant metric is outside this counterexample''s hypotheses; do not overextend the obstruction.", "tests": "experiments/code/geometry_round2_exact.py: exact trace recurrence, first80 Euler exponents and cyclic-label uniqueness through period8; the all-n proof is in frontiers/geometry_round2.md.", "significance": "Separates geometric purity from several tempting but insufficient algebraic and analytic substitutes.", "difficulty": "Elementary construction; applying it to a proposed infinite-dimensional number-field model requires exact axiom matching.", "status": "Explicit proof plus independent parent check; no external novelty review.", "id": "CONN-G001", "provenance_file": "connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl"}','Positive Euler exponents, reciprocal functional equation, rational local polynomials and alternating self-duality do not supply the geometric-monodromy pole control required by DeligneI(3.2). The explicit A=[[2,1],[1,3]] yields both a formal positive zeta with off-circle roots and a genuine constant-arithmetic lisse-sheaf test.','connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-G002','connections/connections.jsonl',48,'Derived lemma under independent review; not assigned literature novelty.','connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-G002", "source_theorems": ["THM-G003", "THM-G004", "THM-G012", "THM-G013"], "kind": "quantified sufficient-condition transfer", "statement": "The inspected even-tensor Euler-product proof needs sublinear excess weight on geometric coinvariants, rather than the whole open-Sp hypothesis as a black box. Coinvariant bounds q^(kβ+Ck), Ck=o(k), give local |α|≤q_x^(β/2+(Ck+1)/(2k)); alternating duality supplies equality.", "compatible_assumptions": "Affine open U0⊂P1/Fq; lisse Qℓ-sheaf, ℓ≠char Fq; perfect alternating pairing to Qℓ(−β); rational local characteristic polynomials; algebraic Frobenius coinvariant eigenvalues with all-conjugate bound for arbitrarily large k. These are explicit hypotheses, not claimed available for classical zeta.", "new_claim_suggested": "Derived sufficient-condition lemma THM-G013: replace exact Sp-invariant Tate pole control by asymptotically Tate even-tensor coinvariants.", "already_proved": "Deligne''s coefficient positivity, cohomological formula and power argument; source-grounded reconstruction of the conditional implication supplied.", "conjectural": "No classical-number-field realization or sublinear tensor-degree bound is known from this campaign. Separate review of the derived lemma remains pending.", "next_step": "Independently check coefficient-field descent, local-factor radius inequality, Hc2 coinvariant identification and all-complex-conjugate quantifiers; then test one non-Sp monodromy family.", "potential_counterexamples": "The constant arithmetic A-sheaf fails the sublinear bound: α+^(2k) produces excess weight linear in k. Bounds with Ck proportional to k do not force purity.", "tests": "Symbolic exponent/logarithm calculation; explicit A tensor eigenvalue growth; no numerical observation substitutes for the limiting proof.", "significance": "Makes the genuinely needed quantitative pole-control input explicit and supplies a sharper target than a vague Frobenius analogy.", "difficulty": "Small derived lemma moderate; constructing useful nontrivial geometric or number-field examples is high difficulty.", "status": "Derived lemma under independent review; not assigned literature novelty.", "id": "CONN-G002", "provenance_file": "connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl"}','The inspected even-tensor Euler-product proof needs sublinear excess weight on geometric coinvariants, rather than the whole open-Sp hypothesis as a black box. Coinvariant bounds q^(kβ+Ck), Ck=o(k), give local |α|≤q_x^(β/2+(Ck+1)/(2k)); alternating duality supplies equality.','connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-G003','connections/connections.jsonl',49,'Documented established relationship; not a novel literature discovery; full technical reconstruction pending.','connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-G003", "source_theorems": ["THM-G008", "THM-G009"], "kind": "source-documented historical technique transfer", "statement": "WeilII §2 applies Hadamard–de la Vallée-Poussin/Mertens positivity to get wq(α)<β+2 on curve Hc1, then geometric product/vanishing-cycle iteration sharpens to the optimal weight bound via errors2^(−k).", "compatible_assumptions": "Smooth curve over Fq, lisse iota-pure sheaf, chosen iota and real weight β. Weight-zero normalization uses twisting; the full proof requires its monodromy and vanishing-cycle hypotheses.", "new_claim_suggested": "For future reverse transfers to analytic number theory, identify an actual contraction of localization error in addition to a positivity inequality.", "already_proved": "Historical transfer explicitly described in WeilII introduction pp139–141 and §2; precise strict bound(2.2.10) and iterative estimate(3.2.4) inspected in the primary source.", "conjectural": "A comparable contraction mechanism for a classical-zeta analytic family is not supplied.", "next_step": "Fully reconstruct the contraction for one explicit sheaf family, preserving the strict initial bound and integer-weight step, before proposing an analytic analogue.", "potential_counterexamples": "Coefficient positivity alone passes the A countermodel and does not provide error contraction; merely reusing a trigonometric positivity polynomial is insufficient.", "tests": "Exact identity3+4cosθ+cos2θ=2(1+cosθ)^2≥0 is a small local check; it does not verify the complete geometric argument.", "significance": "Preserves a mathematically concrete analytic-to-geometric transfer and identifies the extra ingredient needed for its reversal.", "difficulty": "Full source reconstruction substantial; any new reverse transfer very high difficulty.", "status": "Documented established relationship; not a novel literature discovery; full technical reconstruction pending.", "id": "CONN-G003", "provenance_file": "connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl"}','WeilII §2 applies Hadamard–de la Vallée-Poussin/Mertens positivity to get wq(α)<β+2 on curve Hc1, then geometric product/vanishing-cycle iteration sharpens to the optimal weight bound via errors2^(−k).','connections/geometry_round2_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-HF301','connections/connections.jsonl',50,'Established source relationship and independently checked conversion; no novelty claim.','connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-HF301", "source_theorems": ["THM-HF301", "THM-HF303", "THM-HF304", "THM-HF305"], "kind": "source-verified historical theorem chain and parameter normalization", "statement": "deBruijn''s all-zero strip contraction supplies a nonempty downward real-rooted set in Newman''s dampingb. Newman''s measure classification and the Riemann kernel''s super-exponential tail make its cutoff finite; exact kernel substitution gives standardΛ=−4b0.", "compatible_assumptions": "Actual positive even Riemann kernel has every Gaussian tilt integrable and initial Fourierzeros within the critical strip; classification is applied to an even nonnegative finite measure. OriginalkernelF(2u)=2Φ(u) matches the two Fourier scales.", "new_claim_suggested": "Use the explicit convention map in every theorem/experiment rather than treating all deBruijn–Newman parameters as identical.", "already_proved": "Source statements, quartic lower-bound contradiction, includedendpoint and kernel substitution inspected/reconstructed.", "conjectural": "No conclusion that standardΛ≤0 is obtained. These are historical foundations, not the best current upper bound.", "next_step": "Audit any numerical heat-bound transfer against the sign, scale4 and Fourier-variable dilation2 before reusing constants.", "potential_counterexamples": "Quartic kernels can have threshold−∞; finite Gaussian measures may not admit allpositiveheat tilts. Those do not invalidate the Riemann-specific finite-cutoff proof.", "tests": "Primarypageimagesp245,p247,p205; exact coefficient comparison F_Newman(2u)=2Φ_RT(u).", "significance": "Prevents real sign/factor errors and distinguishes existence of a family from existence of a finite threshold.", "difficulty": "Normalization elementary; full classification theorem substantial and not independently audited beyond the recorded scope.", "status": "Established source relationship and independently checked conversion; no novelty claim.", "id": "CONN-HF301", "provenance_file": "connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl"}','deBruijn''s all-zero strip contraction supplies a nonempty downward real-rooted set in Newman''s dampingb. Newman''s measure classification and the Riemann kernel''s super-exponential tail make its cutoff finite; exact kernel substitution gives standardΛ=−4b0.','connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-HF302','connections/connections.jsonl',51,'Derived source-grounded control under independent review; noveltyunassessed.','connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-HF302", "source_theorems": ["THM-HF301", "THM-HF302", "THM-HF306", "THM-HF307", "THM-HF309", "THM-HF310"], "kind": "positive smooth countermodel linking finite positivity and heat thresholds", "statement": "Quartic smoothing of the positive three-atom kernel gives a strictlypositiveevenC∞superGaussian density with finite positive heat threshold while preserving any prescribed finite positive Li-type prefix. It therefore defeats an inference from finite-prefix positivity plus generic kernel regularity to a nonpositive threshold.", "compatible_assumptions": "hε=cεexp(−(u/ε)^4) has imaginary Laplacezeros by deBruijnTheorem1; convolution is an admissible function forTheorem13, with exactinitialstriphalfwidtha. Li-type coefficients are of F(s−1/2), not the classicalRiemannξ.", "new_claim_suggested": "Require genuinely all-n or arithmetic input beyond finite positivity/regularity when proposing a heat-based RH certificate.", "already_proved": "Atomic cutofflogcosha; source-class smoothing; positivefinite cutoff0<Λε≤a²/2; finite-prefix continuity and nonnegative critical-line smoothing contributions. Exacta1/100 first100 coefficients have outward interval enclosures, pending separate arithmetic review.", "conjectural": "The exact smoothed threshold and its convergence tologcosha are not established. No classicalRH result follows.", "next_step": "Independently check the smoothingHadamard-product argument and interval recurrence; investigate an actual global-zero estimate that could control limsup of thresholds.", "potential_counterexamples": "Locallyuniform transforms do not by themselves control all zeros or global threshold limsup. Atoms alone do not meet deBruijn''s integrable-function hypotheses; the explicit smoothing repairs this.", "tests": "experiments/code/heatflow_round2.py; exact finite Taylor interval evidence. Rouché/dominated-convergence argument in audits/heatflow_round2.md is the analytic justification.", "significance": "Supplies an explicit regular positive-kernel negative control rather than only a finite artificial polynomial.", "difficulty": "Auxiliary proof moderate; global heat-threshold convergence is a distinct unresolved task here.", "status": "Derived source-grounded control under independent review; noveltyunassessed.", "id": "CONN-HF302", "provenance_file": "connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl"}','Quartic smoothing of the positive three-atom kernel gives a strictlypositiveevenC∞superGaussian density with finite positive heat threshold while preserving any prescribed finite positive Li-type prefix. It therefore defeats an inference from finite-prefix positivity plus generic kernel regularity to a nonpositive threshold.','connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-HF303','connections/connections.jsonl',52,'Derived auxiliary obstruction under independent review.','connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-HF303", "source_theorems": ["THM-HF301", "THM-HF306", "THM-HF307", "THM-HF308"], "kind": "universal constant sharpness obstruction", "statement": "The coefficient2 in the direct-heat strip formula cannot be increased universally, even for strictlypositiveevenC∞superGaussian densities: chooseasmallwithlogcosha>a²/c and persist the atomic off-axiszero atτ=a²/c in its admissible quartic smoothing.", "compatible_assumptions": "Every smoothed initial transform has all zeros in the exact stripa. At the tested heat time a simple atomic off-axiszero survives for sufficientlysmallε by locallyuniform convergence/Rouché.", "new_claim_suggested": "Any improvement for a particular arithmetic kernel must exploit additional structure, rather than a stronger universal strip-contraction coefficient based only on positivity and regularity.", "already_proved": "Explicit choice/existence inequalities and analytic witness persistence supplied.", "conjectural": "No claim of novelty, optimal constants for the Riemann kernel, or exact smoothed-threshold convergence.", "next_step": "Independent adversarial check of all quantifiers and source-class membership; compare with prior sharpness literature before publication-level novelty assessment.", "potential_counterexamples": "Additional arithmetic hypotheses are outside this universal negative control and may permit improvements for special kernels.", "tests": "No finite numerical sampling can prove this universal obstruction; the proof is analytic in audits/heatflow_round2.md.", "significance": "Rules out a precise family of impossible universal improvements while leaving special arithmetic improvements open.", "difficulty": "Elementary limiting construction once source theorems are fixed; literature identification remains outstanding.", "status": "Derived auxiliary obstruction under independent review.", "id": "CONN-HF303", "provenance_file": "connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl"}','The coefficient2 in the direct-heat strip formula cannot be increased universally, even for strictlypositiveevenC∞superGaussian densities: chooseasmallwithlogcosha>a²/c and persist the atomic off-axiszero atτ=a²/c in its admissible quartic smoothing.','connections/heatflow_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-DIR-HG501','connections/connections.jsonl',53,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_round5_adjudication.md','{"id": "CONN-DIR-HG501", "source_theorems": ["OBS-HG501", "OBS-HR501", "OBS-HR503"], "statement": "A nonlinear positive-real cocycle turns weighted Wiener atom detection into the exact zeta-ratio multiplicity slope; the linear Herglotz term contributes energy at infinity while continuous boundary measure contributes none at first order.", "compatible_assumptions": "Compensated positive Herglotz measure with finite integral(1+gamma²)^-1dmu; fixedPoissoncenterx>0. For xi, RH is needed separately to identify the atomic positive representation and a0.", "already_proved": "Full scalar slope with noninteger atom masses, singular continuous measures and infinite total mass. Two different proofs and Gaussian/Lebesgue controls independently checked.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Exact nonlinear-formula priority; quantitative remainders for diffuse/fractal measures and growing centers. No independent positivity proof for actual xi is supplied.", "next_precise_step": "Give effective remainder under a stated modulus of atom concentration, then verify a natural arithmetic approximation meets it; search exact Hardy/Herglotz antecedents.", "potential_counterexamples": "exp(w²) has nonzero infinity energy despite no zeros. No unrestricted C_b test-convergence assertion is made when Gaussian energy escapes; tests need behavior at infinity. Total-variation convergence to a nonzero atomic limit is impossible for the absolutely continuous epsilon-energy measures.", "tests": "Exact beta profiles, two linear autocorrelation/Wiener normalizations, uniform continuous and infinite-Lebesgue sanity controls; numerical agreement is not used as proof.", "significance": "Reusable analytic identity and exact structural explanation of a multiplicity norm; priority unassessed, no RH progress claim.", "difficulty": "Ordinary harmonic analysis once the compensated tail and boundary limits are treated correctly; effective uniform arithmetic application remains difficult.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_round5_adjudication.md", "provenance_file": "connections/herglotz_semigroup_director_round5.jsonl"}','A nonlinear positive-real cocycle turns weighted Wiener atom detection into the exact zeta-ratio multiplicity slope; the linear Herglotz term contributes energy at infinity while continuous boundary measure contributes none at first order.','connections/herglotz_semigroup_director_round5.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-DIR-XW501','connections/connections.jsonl',54,'adjudicated_scoped_RH_conditional','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_round5_adjudication.md; ratio62_semigroup.md; xi_weighted_semigroup_rt62_xi_semigroup.md','{"id": "CONN-DIR-XW501", "source_theorems": ["OBS-XW501", "OBS-XW502", "OBS-HG501", "PAPER-M001:Hadamard_product_and_Riemann_vonMangoldt"], "statement": "Growing local zero density makes a natural xi-weighted Hardy translation compact, but gamma/product growth then removes every spectral eigenvalue: the actual generator has empty spectrum, while zeros appear in boundary orbit energy and domain obstructions.", "compatible_assumptions": "RH, ordinary right-half-plane Hardy space, the exact cocycle F(w)/F(w+tau), maximal C0 generator domain. These are not interchangeable with de Branges or other proposed spectral spaces.", "already_proved": "Contraction, strong continuity, positive-time compactness/injectivity/quasinilpotence, entire generator resolvent, and exact kernel nondifferentiability coefficient.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Historical priority and whether a different explicitly defined Hilbert-space realization can have a meaningful nonempty self-adjoint spectrum with the arithmetic trace formula.", "next_precise_step": "For one proposed replacement space state its norm and domain, prove closed self-adjointness and a genuine zero-count/trace identity; compare the current empty-spectrum control before asserting zero eigenvalues.", "potential_counterexamples": "Unweighted translation is noncompact; a finite polynomial imaginary-zero product need not have the growing-density compactness input. A formal differential expression does not specify a generator domain.", "tests": "Boundary-window product decay, finite-output Hilbert–Schmidt cutoff, iterated-eigenfunction contradiction and direct all-lambda resolvent identities are analytic checks; no zeta numerics establish RH.", "significance": "Precise negative knowledge for one spectral construction and a positive link to the energy identity, not a blanket obstruction to Hilbert–Polya.", "difficulty": "Self-contained given standard Hardy/product/counting inputs; constructing a useful alternative arithmetic operator is much harder.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped_RH_conditional", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_round5_adjudication.md; ratio62_semigroup.md; xi_weighted_semigroup_rt62_xi_semigroup.md", "provenance_file": "connections/herglotz_semigroup_director_round5.jsonl"}','Growing local zero density makes a natural xi-weighted Hardy translation compact, but gamma/product growth then removes every spectral eigenvalue: the actual generator has empty spectrum, while zeros appear in boundary orbit energy and domain obstructions.','connections/herglotz_semigroup_director_round5.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-DIR-HR501','connections/connections.jsonl',55,'adjudicated_scoped; no publication novelty claim','audits/adversarial_reviews/horizontal_ratio_slope_director_adjudication_round5.md','{"id": "CONN-DIR-HR501", "source_theorems": ["OBS-HR501", "OBS-HR502", "OBS-HR503", "PAPER-C103:Proposition2"], "statement": "The exact first-order horizontal zeta-ratio norm is a weighted multiplicity statistic under RH; an order-one Schur/Poisson mass identity connects the published approximation norm to local beta-integral profiles at zeros.", "compatible_assumptions": "RH, fixed actual xi zero set, both signs counted separately, positive real epsilon→0, complete real-line Poisson weight. No moving zero configuration, spacing or simplicity assumption.", "already_proved": "Scoped independent reconstruction of the exact slope and its minimum iff simplicity, with two different global-tail arguments and a negative control.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Historical priority and effective remainder; whether any independently established estimate can force the minimum for actual zeta remains entirely unresolved.", "next_precise_step": "Search later ratio/Hardy literature; derive an explicit oepsilon remainder under stated quantitative zero-gap/multiplicity/tail hypotheses.", "potential_counterexamples": "F=exp(w²) shows failure if order-one paired-product mass identity is omitted; finite epsilon agreement cannot exclude a high multiple zero.", "tests": "Exact beta-integral identities; rational finite paired-zero model stress tests; ordinary numerics only as checks, not proof.", "significance": "Reusable RH-conditional multiplicity diagnostic and resolution of a precise source question at the reconstruction level; novelty unassessed.", "difficulty": "Proof is self-contained given classical xi product and Poisson facts; effective rates and arithmetic simplicity remain difficult.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped; no publication novelty claim", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/horizontal_ratio_slope_director_adjudication_round5.md", "provenance_file": "connections/horizontal_ratio_slope_director_round5.jsonl"}','The exact first-order horizontal zeta-ratio norm is a weighted multiplicity statistic under RH; an order-one Schur/Poisson mass identity connects the published approximation norm to local beta-integral profiles at zeros.','connections/horizontal_ratio_slope_director_round5.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-RI301','connections/connections.jsonl',56,'Complete auxiliary proof plus independent parent review; separate third review pending. Prior realization theory acknowledged; novelty unassessed.','connections/inner_round2.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-RI301", "source_theorems": ["THM-RI301", "THM-RI302", "THM-RI304", "THM-RI305", "THM-RI306"], "kind": "exact passive-realization to closed-spectrum counting transfer", "statement": "The finite passive transfer pattern from Tabak–MabuchiEq41 becomes S0(k)=I−iG(k−Ω+iG*G/2)^−1G* under s=−ik. A specified closed edge-plus-state boundary operator realizes it self-adjointly; dark-state decomposition and determinant phase budget then give the one-sided curvature boundΔN<3E+M.", "compatible_assumptions": "Finite HermitianΩ onC^M, arbitrary finiteG:C^M→C^E, positive finite edge lengths, constant unitary closureC, fixed full operator/domain at all heights. Darkstates are explicitly retained in totalM. The prescribed upper-half-plane factor class has an explicit cascade Ω,G realization.", "new_claim_suggested": "A finite auxiliary passive boundary model matching the positive Riemann–vonMangoldt curvature with o(K) errors must satisfy liminf(3E_K+M_K)/K≥log2/π.", "already_proved": "Full density/adjoint/compactness proof; factor-cascade elimination including centers; general visible/dark decomposition; inner identity and phase budget; exact count including endpoint/dark multiplicities; curvature/error arithmetic.", "conjectural": "No approximation of actual zero counts is constructed; no universal characterization of arbitrary real-axis unitaryS(k) is claimed. Literature novelty remains unassessed.", "next_step": "Independent third reconstruction, then apply the explicit full-domain test to one proposed RH spectral model and computeE,M with all dark modes retained.", "potential_counterexamples": "Wrong-half-plane inverse factors are real-axis unitary but have negative phase velocity. Infinite-state or nonrational systems lie outside the finite-degree theorem. Removing dark states from the count invalidates the identity.", "tests": "Exact Gaussian-rational noncommutingE2/M3 cascade, arbitraryHermitianmodel, dark-real-pole removal and rankG1/M2 visible-state example in experiments/code/factored_inner_round2.py; proofs in the campaign.", "significance": "Provides an actual unbounded boundary realization and a quantitative auxiliary-state cost, rather than a formal unitary secular equation.", "difficulty": "Auxiliary operator proof moderate; assessing a genuinely proposed number-field realization requires substantial additional mathematics.", "status": "Complete auxiliary proof plus independent parent review; separate third review pending. Prior realization theory acknowledged; novelty unassessed.", "id": "CONN-RI301", "provenance_file": "connections/inner_round2.jsonl"}','The finite passive transfer pattern from Tabak–MabuchiEq41 becomes S0(k)=I−iG(k−Ω+iG*G/2)^−1G* under s=−ik. A specified closed edge-plus-state boundary operator realizes it self-adjointly; dark-state decomposition and determinant phase budget then give the one-sided curvature boundΔN<3E+M.','connections/inner_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-RI302','connections/connections.jsonl',57,'Independently checked by child and parent; no error in a cited theorem alleged.','connections/inner_round2.jsonl','{"connection_id": "CONN-RI302", "source_theorems": ["THM-D205", "THM-RI307", "THM-RI305"], "kind": "domain-level barrier to invalid theorem chaining", "statement": "The finite-defect3d relative-count theorem requires a densely defined common symmetric restriction. For the scalar boundary-coupled auxiliary model versus periodic derivative⊕[d], common domains imposez=0, so no such dense common restriction exists. The auxiliary degree cannot be erased by treating this as an edge-only domain perturbation.", "compatible_assumptions": "Both full operators are genuinely selfadjoint on the enlarged L2⊕C space, but the required dense-common-S hypothesis fails explicitly. This is a negative hypothesis match, not an application of the interlacing theorem.", "new_claim_suggested": "Track the full auxiliary Hilbert space and use the direct rational-inner/dark-state count when the densely-defined common-S interface fails.", "already_proved": "Exact domain-intersection witness and ambient closure obstruction; general versionGq=0; the full boundary-model count charges all finite states.", "conjectural": "A symmetric-linear-relation formulation could recover a different relative-count theorem but was not established in this campaign.", "next_step": "Audit any claimed extension-theoretic realization for density of the proposed common domain before assigning its deficiency or dropping auxiliary states.", "potential_counterexamples": "G=0 makes the models decoupled and the domain obstruction disappears; it does not justify the claim forG≠0.", "tests": "Scalarγ≠0 versusγ0 dark-state control and explicit common-domain calculation; no numerical evidence needed.", "significance": "Prevents a stronger but invalid model-cost conclusion from an otherwise correct finite-defect theorem.", "difficulty": "Elementary exact counterexample; a general linear-relation extension would require new source work.", "status": "Independently checked by child and parent; no error in a cited theorem alleged.", "id": "CONN-RI302", "provenance_file": "connections/inner_round2.jsonl"}','The finite-defect3d relative-count theorem requires a densely defined common symmetric restriction. For the scalar boundary-coupled auxiliary model versus periodic derivative⊕[d], common domains imposez=0, so no such dense common restriction exists. The auxiliary degree cannot be erased by treating this as an edge-only domain perturbation.','connections/inner_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-LATEST62-Q1501','connections/connections.jsonl',58,'adjudicated_scoped_source_dependent_classical_transfer','proposals/independent_campaigns/mertens_shifted_q1_latest62_round5.md','{"id": "CONN-LATEST62-Q1501", "source_theorems": ["LEM-LATEST62-Q1501", "THM-LATEST62-Q1502", "OBS-MERTENS-Q1-ASYM", "OBS-HR501"], "statement": "A full dyadic reciprocal first moment away from the twist and a pointwise optimized local Perron shift prove the classical q1 rate for the prescribed shifted Mobius array.", "already_proved": "Uniform twisted bound for every cutoffx>=N, low/middle/high height split, classical rate and exact q1 leading coefficient after the separately checked ratio slope.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Historical priority, unrestricted optimality and effective constants. Complete recent input proofs were not independently audited end to end.", "next_precise_step": "Compare exact prescribed-array antecedents and independently audit the recent reciprocal-first-moment dependency; propagate effective constants.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped_source_dependent_classical_transfer", "evidence": "proposals/independent_campaigns/mertens_shifted_q1_latest62_round5.md", "provenance_file": "connections/mertens_shifted_q1_latest62_round5.jsonl", "original_status": "conditional_proof_candidate_pending_independent_review", "compatible_assumptions": "RH; exact BFH first-reciprocal and Mertens inputs, Bui-Florea uniform pointwise estimate, fixedA>C, full-height norm; no short-window moment extrapolation.", "potential_counterexamples": "Generic envelope-only Fourier multiplier bound fails by modulation; using Proposition14 at the smaller shift would be invalid, so the proof uses Proposition13 and a new intermediate contour.", "tests": "Two independent contour/source reconstructions plus director verification of all-x Abel eligibility and exact source regimes.", "significance": "Explicit source-dependent classical approximation improvement relative to the quoted2010 bound; no current-best or novelty claim.", "difficulty": "Uniform analytic contour proof using substantial declared source estimates.", "status_update_evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_round5_adjudication.md; threshold62_q1_twisted_perron_review.md; ratio62_q1_mertens_shifted.md"}','A full dyadic reciprocal first moment away from the twist and a pointwise optimized local Perron shift prove the classical q1 rate for the prescribed shifted Mobius array.','connections/mertens_shifted_q1_latest62_round5.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-LATEST62-W501','connections/connections.jsonl',59,'scoped_reconstruction_priority_unassessed','proposals/independent_campaigns/mertens_shifted_weighted_latest62_round5.md','{"id": "CONN-LATEST62-W501", "source_theorems": ["THM-LATEST62-006", "THM-C103-P1P3", "THM-WC-R2-1", "LEM-LATEST62-W501", "THM-LATEST62-W502"], "statement": "Bui–Florea–Heycock''s RH-conditional Mertens estimate and Balazard–de Roton''s quotient bound give a full-sequence rate for a classical shifted Möbius array in the q>1 weighted criterion.", "compatible_assumptions": "RH; explicit Theorem 1.4 k=1 Mertens bound with constant C; fixed A>C; fixed real q>1. Hardy converse uses no Mertens estimate.", "already_proved": "Conditional transfer by exact partial summation and a concave tangent estimate. Supremum multiplier suffices for integer q≥2; Fourier Plancherel and Lindelöf extend the forward transfer to q>1.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Independent proof adjudication, wider priority, optimum weighted distance, and q=1 transfer for the new shift.", "next_precise_step": "Test the q=1 height-weight barrier with the exact Fourier transform of the Abel tail, and independently verify the source constant and the admissible q range.", "status": "scoped_reconstruction_priority_unassessed", "evidence": "proposals/independent_campaigns/mertens_shifted_weighted_latest62_round5.md", "provenance_file": "connections/mertens_shifted_weighted_latest62_round5.jsonl"}','Bui–Florea–Heycock''s RH-conditional Mertens estimate and Balazard–de Roton''s quotient bound give a full-sequence rate for a classical shifted Möbius array in the q>1 weighted criterion.','connections/mertens_shifted_weighted_latest62_round5.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-MONT73-A006-A003','connections/connections.jsonl',60,'Primarypassagescomparedandidentityalgebrareconstructed; noarithmeticnewboundclaimed','audits/montgomery1973_round2.md','{"id": "CONN-MONT73-A006-A003", "source_papers": ["PAPER-E009", "PAPER-A006", "PAPER-A003"], "source_locators": ["MontgomeryEq18,p185,Cor1/2pp182,191–192", "BGSTBTheorem1pp1–2,Lemma3pp3–4,Lemma5p6", "Lamzouri§3pp12–13,Lemma3.2"], "claim": "Classicalreal-ordinatepaircorrelationandnonnegativesinc-squaremultiplicityboundisextendedbykeepingcomplexzerosintheprimeformulaandthenreplacingtermwisepositivitywithafiniteconjugation-invarianttensorinequality.", "verified_compatible_assumptions": "BGSTBFBequalsMontgomeryFMonRH; offRHdifferentfunctions. LamzourifixedtestsQ,Qsecondderivativeareeven,smooth,compactsupported,validforBGSTBLemma5.", "already_proved": "Original2/3simpleunderRH; BGSTBunconditionalcomplexpairformula; LamzouriunconditionalsimplecriticalproportionasspecifiedinPAPER-A003.", "new_claim_suggested": "Effectivefiniteheightfixed-testcertificateswithallconstantsmadeexplicit; notyetprovedhere.", "next_step": "TrackBGSTBTheorem1constantsandLipschitz/testnormsinLemma5,applyseparatelytoQandQsecondderivative.", "counterexample_risks": ["Complexkerneltermsarenotpointwisenonnegative.", "Changingtestuniformitydoesnotfollowfromfixed-testO_r.", "Originalendpointuniformitynotavailablewithoutlaterinput."], "verification": "Primarypassagescomparedandidentityalgebrareconstructed; noarithmeticnewboundclaimed", "evidence": "audits/montgomery1973_round2.md", "novelty": "Historicaldependencyandknownmechanisms; no noveltyclaim", "provenance_file": "connections/montgomery_original_round2.jsonl"}','Classicalreal-ordinatepaircorrelationandnonnegativesinc-squaremultiplicityboundisextendedbykeepingcomplexzerosintheprimeformulaandthenreplacingtermwisepositivitywithafiniteconjugation-invarianttensorinequality.','connections/montgomery_original_round2.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-ROOTED-CUE-CLOSED-WINDOW-ARITHMETIC-GAP','connections/connections.jsonl',61,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_cue_windows_round13.md','{"id": "CONN-ROOTED-CUE-CLOSED-WINDOW-ARITHMETIC-GAP", "sources": ["THM-ROOTED-CUE-JOINT-CLOSED-MOMENT-WINDOW", "THM-HLZ-FINITE-BAND-MOMENT-WINDOW", "THM-ROOTED-CUE-FIRST-FREQUENCY-CORRECTION"], "statement": "The intrinsic closed CUE window gives a higher-support comparison formula, while the arithmetic length threshold differs.", "hypotheses": "Fixed band and fixed moment degree; intrinsic rb≤1, source arithmetic rb<1/2 under RH.", "already_proved": "Exact complementary determinant and first intrinsic correction.", "conjectural": "Arithmetic moments exceeding the source length window.", "next_step": "Estimate the long pure fourth arm before seeking a full fixed-band comparison.", "tests": "Tagged endpoint check, exact rational projection and continuum chamber certificates.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_cue_windows_round13.md", "provenance_file": "connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl"}','The intrinsic closed CUE window gives a higher-support comparison formula, while the arithmetic length threshold differs.','connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-GRID-TIGHTNESS-CLASSICAL-MODULUS','connections/connections.jsonl',62,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_two_scale_round13.md','{"id": "CONN-GRID-TIGHTNESS-CLASSICAL-MODULUS", "sources": ["THM-GRID-TWO-SCALE-UNIVERSAL-TIGHTNESS", "THM-GR1974-GRR-MODULUS", "THM-BILLINGSLEY1968-C-TIGHTNESS-AND-TRIANGLE", "THM-SHRINKING-BAND-BROWNIAN-PROCESS"], "statement": "A classical modulus inequality and spike mechanism recover the exact universal parameter threshold once a local fine increment envelope is available.", "hypotheses": "Deterministic grids, both increment bounds and tight initial values; arithmetic application assumes RH.", "already_proved": "Uniform interpolation and modulus, sharp worst-case obstruction, and the M>2 consequence for a=b=2.", "conjectural": "Arithmetic fine bound or effective path-law rates in other regimes.", "next_step": "Establish the fine increment estimate appropriate to a new weighted process.", "tests": "Independent dyadic and GRR calculations and the local Lean scalar check.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_two_scale_round13.md", "provenance_file": "connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl"}','A classical modulus inequality and spike mechanism recover the exact universal parameter threshold once a local fine increment envelope is available.','connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-HR-BANDLIMITED-AVERAGE-LOG-TAIL','connections/connections.jsonl',63,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_hughes_rudnick_whole_round13.md','{"id": "CONN-HR-BANDLIMITED-AVERAGE-LOG-TAIL", "sources": ["THM-HR-REPAIRED-FINITE-GAUSSIAN-MOMENTS", "THM-HR-OSCILLATORY-PRINTED-WEIGHT-WINDOW"], "statement": "Bandlimiting removes unmatched prime products, while the full statistic''s smooth gamma term needs separate log-tail integrability.", "hypotheses": "Printed weight class and strict Fourier window in the pinned Hughes–Rudnick journal edition.", "already_proved": "The oscillatory result on the printed class, the fixed-weight counterexample and repaired finite moments.", "conjectural": "A full Gaussian law for a fixed test is outside this comparison.", "next_step": "Track actual weight hypotheses in applications of the finite-moment theorem.", "tests": "Exact shifted log asymptotic and a positive fixed weighted translate series.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_hughes_rudnick_whole_round13.md", "provenance_file": "connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl"}','Bandlimiting removes unmatched prime products, while the full statistic''s smooth gamma term needs separate log-tail integrability.','connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-PURE-FOURTH-SMOOTH-CSTAR-EDGE','connections/connections.jsonl',64,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/uniform99_fixed_sequence_adjudication.md','{"id": "CONN-PURE-FOURTH-SMOOTH-CSTAR-EDGE", "sources": ["OBS-HLZ-FOURTH-PURE-ARM-REDUCTION", "LEM-HLZ-ONE-SIDED-LONG-CONTINUOUS", "LEM-HLZ-SMOOTH-REFLECTED-SADDLE", "LEM-HLZ-REFLECTED-EDGE-FIXED-SEQUENCE", "OPEN-HLZ-PURE-FOURTH-CSTAR-CANCELLATION"], "statement": "The arithmetic fourth-moment extension reduces to the signed nonprincipal sum for the fixed sequence d_2*(Lambda log²).", "hypotheses": "RH for the target weighted-zero theorem, fixed 1/8<b<1/6, compact comparable-height tapers and strict-tail transfer.", "already_proved": "Mixed arms, asymmetric continuous estimate, smooth saddle and exact divisor removal.", "conjectural": "Re E_Cstar=o(T log⁴T) and hence the long pure and real fourth moments.", "next_step": "Exploit the sign and four-prime outer structure in the surviving Mangoldt convolution.", "tests": "Independent contour/error reviews and Poisson and Hurwitz–Mellin identities.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/uniform99_fixed_sequence_adjudication.md", "provenance_file": "connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl"}','The arithmetic fourth-moment extension reduces to the signed nonprincipal sum for the fixed sequence d_2*(Lambda log²).','connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-PETROV-EXACT-TAIL-AND-FORMAL-CUE-WINDOW','connections/connections.jsonl',65,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_petrov_round13.md','{"id": "CONN-PETROV-EXACT-TAIL-AND-FORMAL-CUE-WINDOW", "sources": ["PAPER-GEOMETRY102-PETROV2026", "LEM-PETROV-ROOTED-CUE-EXACT-FACTOR-BRIDGE", "OBS-PETROV-ROOTED-CUE-GRAM-QUADRATIC-MISMATCH", "THM-ROOTED-CUE-INTEGER-RANK-WINDOW"], "statement": "The exact tilted factorization gives an alternate intrinsic CUE interface and requires both the Gram and tail factors even inside the moment window.", "hypotheses": "Fixed rank and finite exponential Laurent symbol. Real-axis positivity and the optional chart are distinct assertions.", "already_proved": "Exact factor bridge, strict quadratic gap, and a positive-axis failure of optional chart invertibility.", "conjectural": "Uniform finite-dimensional approximation of the tail quotient beyond low orders.", "next_step": "Control the exact tail quotient uniformly in N and bounded real z while tracking the higher Fourier chambers.", "tests": "Independent operator matching and exact rational Gram, Jacobi and chart extraction.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_petrov_round13.md", "provenance_file": "connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl"}','The exact tilted factorization gives an alternate intrinsic CUE interface and requires both the Gram and tail factors even inside the moment window.','connections/research_round13_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-ROOTED-CUE-FORMAL-ZERO-FINITE-HANKEL-ORDER','connections/connections.jsonl',66,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_quantitative_rmt_round14.md','{"id": "CONN-ROOTED-CUE-FORMAL-ZERO-FINITE-HANKEL-ORDER", "sources": ["OBS-ROOTED-CUE-ALL-RANK-FINITE-SQUARE-BARRIER", "THM-ROOTED-CUE-HANKEL-WITNESS-DEGREE-BOUND", "THM-ROOTED-CUE-RANK-ONE-HERMITE-WITNESS", "CERT-ROOTED-CUE-RANK-ONE-HANKEL-FIXTURES"], "statement": "A real zero of the extrapolating series yields an explicit finite negative Hankel witness, and at rank one the Jacobi matrix gives the least order.", "hypotheses": "Fixed rank and fixed positive band. All positivity tests concern formal moments.", "already_proved": "Explicit upper degree, strict rank-one threshold and independently replayed exact fixtures.", "conjectural": "The least witness order for ranks exceeding one.", "next_step": "Analyze higher-rank signed Gaussian-polynomial forms and compare their least order to the first raw moment crossing.", "tests": "Two Taylor polynomials, Cauchy bounds, Hermite recurrence and exact rational fixtures.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_quantitative_rmt_round14.md", "provenance_file": "connections/research_round14_connections.jsonl"}','A real zero of the extrapolating series yields an explicit finite negative Hankel witness, and at rank one the Jacobi matrix gives the least order.','connections/research_round14_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-PETROV-FINITE-SCHUR-TRUE-CUTOFF','connections/connections.jsonl',67,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_quantitative_rmt_round14.md','{"id": "CONN-PETROV-FINITE-SCHUR-TRUE-CUTOFF", "sources": ["LEM-PETROV-ROOTED-CUE-EXACT-FACTOR-BRIDGE", "LEM-PETROV-ROOTED-CUE-FINITE-SCHUR-TAIL", "THM-PETROV-ROOTED-CUE-TRUE-CUTOFF-CONTINUUM-GRAM", "LEM-PETROV-ROOTED-CUE-FACTORIAL-HANKEL-TRUNCATION", "OBS-PETROV-ROOTED-CUE-GRAM-QUADRATIC-MISMATCH"], "statement": "The exact tilted-to-ambient tail ratio has a positive finite Schur formula. The normalized Gram has a genuine cutoff rather than the oriented formal kernel.", "hypotheses": "Real compact parameter intervals, fixed rank and positive band for uniform estimates.", "already_proved": "Exact finite quotient, positive uniform bounds, continuum Gram and factorial tail truncation.", "conjectural": "Descriptions of higher frequency chambers for the exact rooted law.", "next_step": "Track the actual shifts and cutoff changes beyond the coefficient window.", "tests": "Triangular support, finite Jacobi, compact compression and weighted Fourier convolution.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_quantitative_rmt_round14.md", "provenance_file": "connections/research_round14_connections.jsonl"}','The exact tilted-to-ambient tail ratio has a positive finite Schur formula. The normalized Gram has a genuine cutoff rather than the oriented formal kernel.','connections/research_round14_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-CSTAR-GCD-STRATA-AND-PRIME-WINDOW','connections/connections.jsonl',68,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_arithmetic_strata_round14.md','{"id": "CONN-CSTAR-GCD-STRATA-AND-PRIME-WINDOW", "sources": ["LEM-CSTAR-EFFECTIVE-MODULUS-AND-SHORT-FACTOR", "LEM-CSTAR-SHARED-FACTORS-AND-HIGHER-POWERS", "LEM-CSTAR-ALL-PRIME-SQUARES-BELOW-9-17", "LEM-CSTAR-GCD-RESOLVED-INVERSE-PRIME-WINDOWS", "LEM-CSTAR-KOROLEV-POINTWISE-INVERSE-PRIME-BAND", "OBS-CSTAR-CHARACTER-TWIST-ZERO-RESIDUES", "OPEN-HLZ-PURE-FOURTH-CSTAR-CANCELLATION"], "statement": "Opening the single Mangoldt convolution retains exact gcds and isolates strata with unconditional savings. Freezing the prime factor avoids character-zero residues in a full-sequence divisor transform.", "hypotheses": "Compact comparable heights, bounded four-prime-supported outer coefficients and a fixed taper chosen for the strict margins. RH is needed for transfer to the weighted fourth moment.", "already_proved": "Short, shared, and higher-power removals, complete square removal for θ<9/17 and the stated local genuine-prime regions.", "conjectural": "The residual signed estimate and the corresponding arithmetic fourth-moment limit.", "next_step": "Estimate the prime scales outside the verified regions or bound their signed aggregate directly.", "tests": "Independent centered divisor transforms, rational quadratic prefixes, and common-endpoint averaged inverse-prime bounds.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_arithmetic_strata_round14.md", "provenance_file": "connections/research_round14_connections.jsonl"}','Opening the single Mangoldt convolution retains exact gcds and isolates strata with unconditional savings. Freezing the prime factor avoids character-zero residues in a full-sequence divisor transform.','connections/research_round14_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-MELLIN-RAW-HEIGHT-AND-STRIP-TRACE','connections/connections.jsonl',69,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_mellin_explicit_formula_round15.md','{"id": "CONN-MELLIN-RAW-HEIGHT-AND-STRIP-TRACE", "sources": ["PAPER-L002", "OBS-BL-RAW-HEIGHT-SMOOTH-COUNTEREXAMPLE", "THM-MELLIN-STRIP-SOBOLEV-ZERO-TRACE", "THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ZERO-TRACE", "OBS-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-SMOOTH-STRICT-INCLUSION", "LEM-BL-FINITE-CUTOFF-COMPENSATOR"], "statement": "The auxiliary raw-height assertion can fail for a smooth function. Two sufficient area-norm hypotheses give absolute traces and ordinary compensated formulas, and the finite cutoff has a separate correction.", "hypotheses": "Pinned author manuscript for both source findings; continuous functions with the stated value and strip hypotheses for the repairs.", "already_proved": "Counterexample, two sufficient trace classes, smooth strict inclusion, and exact finite compensator.", "conjectural": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "next_step": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "source_theorems": ["PAPER-L002", "OBS-BL-RAW-HEIGHT-SMOOTH-COUNTEREXAMPLE", "THM-MELLIN-STRIP-SOBOLEV-ZERO-TRACE", "THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ZERO-TRACE", "OBS-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-SMOOTH-STRICT-INCLUSION", "LEM-BL-FINITE-CUTOFF-COMPENSATOR"], "source_claims": [{"id": "PAPER-L002", "locator": "sources/uniform121_bombieri_lagarias/bombieri_lagarias_author.pdf · pp. 5–6 and p. 8, (3.5)"}, {"id": "OBS-BL-RAW-HEIGHT-SMOOTH-COUNTEREXAMPLE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_mellin_explicit_formula_round15.md · A fixed smooth witness for which the stated height limit fails"}, {"id": "THM-MELLIN-STRIP-SOBOLEV-ZERO-TRACE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_mellin_explicit_formula_round15.md · A sufficient strip-Sobolev condition"}, {"id": "THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ZERO-TRACE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_mellin_explicit_formula_round15.md · A weaker critical logarithmic class"}, {"id": "OBS-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-SMOOTH-STRICT-INCLUSION", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_mellin_explicit_formula_round15.md · A weaker critical logarithmic class"}, {"id": "LEM-BL-FINITE-CUTOFF-COMPENSATOR", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_mellin_explicit_formula_round15.md · A separate finite-cutoff identity and why the main theorem survives"}], "compatible_assumptions": "Pinned author manuscript for both source findings; continuous functions with the stated value and strip hypotheses for the repairs.", "new_claim_suggested": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "next_precise_step": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "potential_counterexamples": "The literal value and local bounds already allow the smooth raw-height failure. The compact jump tests lie outside the strip repairs.", "significance": "Validates a precise test class and an explicit truncation error for zero-trace calculations.", "difficulty": "Moderate for sufficiency using standard analytic estimates. The signed endpoint requires further control.", "tests": "Populated zero cells, disk mean values, Dini control, Fourier carrier estimates, and exact finite integration.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_mellin_explicit_formula_round15.md", "novelty_claim": false, "provenance_file": "connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl", "original_status": "adjudicated_scoped", "later_signed_resolution": "Round 16 proves inclusive symmetric raw-height convergence at p=0 with local H¹, including the smooth p=3 absolute-divergence witness, and separate half-axis convergence for p>1. A separate p=3 continuous compact cusp yields signed divergence outside this local class and the literal manuscript class.", "later_signed_claim_ids": ["THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-STRIP-SYMMETRIC-EXPLICIT-FORMULA", "THM-MELLIN-LOG-SIGNED-HALF-AXIS-CONVERGENCE", "LEM-BL-LITERAL-TEST-CLASS-LOCAL-MELLIN-H1", "OBS-MELLIN-LOG-SIGNED-BOUNDARY-CUSP"], "latest_signed_log_boundary": "Round 17 closes the weaker logarithmic-weight question for universal ordinary symmetric summation in the stated class. The critical weight suffices and one smooth witness defeats every strict weakening. Weaker local conditions and the separate half-axis threshold remain independent.", "latest_signed_log_claim_ids": ["LEM-MELLIN-NEGATIVE-LOG-SHARP-INVERSION-PACKET", "OBS-MELLIN-ALL-NEGATIVE-LOG-SIGNED-DIVERGENCE", "THM-MELLIN-EXACT-SIGNED-LOG-BOUNDARY"], "status_update_evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_negative_mellin_round17.md"}','The auxiliary raw-height assertion can fail for a smooth function. Two sufficient area-norm hypotheses give absolute traces and ordinary compensated formulas, and the finite cutoff has a separate correction.','connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ABSOLUTE-ENDPOINT','connections/connections.jsonl',70,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_critical_endpoint_round15.md','{"id": "CONN-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ABSOLUTE-ENDPOINT", "sources": ["THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ZERO-TRACE", "OBS-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ENDPOINT-ABSOLUTE-DIVERGENCE", "PAPER-GEO82-MANGOLDT1905"], "statement": "Universal absolute zero sampling holds for p>3 and fails at p=3 and below in the stated logarithmic scale.", "hypotheses": "Original endpoint value bounds, logarithmically weighted strip area norm and actual nontrivial zeros with multiplicity.", "already_proved": "Sufficient p>3 repair and a smooth p=3 absolute-trace counterexample.", "conjectural": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "next_step": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "source_theorems": ["THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ZERO-TRACE", "OBS-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ENDPOINT-ABSOLUTE-DIVERGENCE", "PAPER-GEO82-MANGOLDT1905"], "source_claims": [{"id": "THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ZERO-TRACE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_mellin_explicit_formula_round15.md · A weaker critical logarithmic class"}, {"id": "OBS-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ENDPOINT-ABSOLUTE-DIVERGENCE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_critical_endpoint_round15.md · Exact assertion"}, {"id": "PAPER-GEO82-MANGOLDT1905", "locator": "von Mangoldt (1905), zero-counting asymptotic as used in audits/adversarial_reviews/director_critical_endpoint_round15.md"}], "compatible_assumptions": "Original endpoint value bounds, logarithmically weighted strip area norm and actual nontrivial zeros with multiplicity.", "new_claim_suggested": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "next_precise_step": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "potential_counterexamples": "The finite-norm p=3 example rules out a universal absolute trace, including all weaker p≤3 weights in this scale.", "significance": "Identifies the exact threshold for universal absolute sampling in this logarithmic family.", "difficulty": "The absolute endpoint uses a probabilistic construction. A signed example or convergence proof remains substantial.", "tests": "Weighted synthesis, dyadic zero counts, two probability bounds and a tail zero–one law.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_critical_endpoint_round15.md", "novelty_claim": false, "provenance_file": "connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl", "original_status": "adjudicated_scoped", "later_signed_resolution": "Round 16 proves inclusive symmetric raw-height convergence at p=0 with local H¹, including the smooth p=3 absolute-divergence witness, and separate half-axis convergence for p>1. A separate p=3 continuous compact cusp yields signed divergence outside this local class and the literal manuscript class.", "later_signed_claim_ids": ["THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-STRIP-SYMMETRIC-EXPLICIT-FORMULA", "THM-MELLIN-LOG-SIGNED-HALF-AXIS-CONVERGENCE", "LEM-BL-LITERAL-TEST-CLASS-LOCAL-MELLIN-H1", "OBS-MELLIN-LOG-SIGNED-BOUNDARY-CUSP"], "latest_signed_log_boundary": "Round 17 closes the weaker logarithmic-weight question for universal ordinary symmetric summation in the stated class. The critical weight suffices and one smooth witness defeats every strict weakening. Weaker local conditions and the separate half-axis threshold remain independent.", "latest_signed_log_claim_ids": ["LEM-MELLIN-NEGATIVE-LOG-SHARP-INVERSION-PACKET", "OBS-MELLIN-ALL-NEGATIVE-LOG-SIGNED-DIVERGENCE", "THM-MELLIN-EXACT-SIGNED-LOG-BOUNDARY"], "status_update_evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_negative_mellin_round17.md"}','Universal absolute zero sampling holds for p>3 and fails at p=3 and below in the stated logarithmic scale.','connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-PHASE-AND-COMPATIBILITY','connections/connections.jsonl',71,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md','{"id": "CONN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-PHASE-AND-COMPATIBILITY", "sources": ["OPEN-HLZ-PURE-FOURTH-CSTAR-CANCELLATION", "LEM-CSTAR-GCD-RESOLVED-INVERSE-PRIME-WINDOWS", "OBS-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-PROGRESSION-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "OPEN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-MOVING-PHASE-SQUARE"], "statement": "A Mellin representation isolates a genuine moving additive phase. Abstract row-wise progression norms do not control it without further structure.", "hypotheses": "Remaining genuine-prime blocks, coprime prime factor, exact divisor gcd, and compact taper.", "already_proved": "Sufficiency of the square target and a norm-only countermodel with inconsistent CRT marginals.", "conjectural": "A bound for genuine primes in the required moving Fourier mode.", "next_step": "Estimate the square or the prescribed signed projection using common-sequence structure.", "source_theorems": ["OPEN-HLZ-PURE-FOURTH-CSTAR-CANCELLATION", "LEM-CSTAR-GCD-RESOLVED-INVERSE-PRIME-WINDOWS", "OBS-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-PROGRESSION-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "OPEN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-MOVING-PHASE-SQUARE"], "source_claims": [{"id": "OPEN-HLZ-PURE-FOURTH-CSTAR-CANCELLATION", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/prime98_fixed_arithmetic_sequence.md"}, {"id": "LEM-CSTAR-GCD-RESOLVED-INVERSE-PRIME-WINDOWS", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_arithmetic_strata_round14.md · Divisor Voronoi and averaged inverse-prime bounds"}, {"id": "OBS-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-PROGRESSION-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md · An exact limitation of two progression norms"}, {"id": "OPEN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-MOVING-PHASE-SQUARE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md · The exact prime form"}], "compatible_assumptions": "Remaining genuine-prime blocks, coprime prime factor, exact divisor gcd, and compact taper.", "new_claim_suggested": "A bound for genuine primes in the required moving Fourier mode.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "A bound for genuine primes in the required moving Fourier mode.", "next_precise_step": "Estimate the square or the prescribed signed projection using common-sequence structure.", "potential_counterexamples": "Positive centered rows with small maximum errors and ideal variance can carry a large phase projection. The row model fails the compatibility test for a common sequence.", "significance": "Separates established prime windows from the remaining long-prime step in the fourth-moment reduction.", "difficulty": "High. The target requires cancellation in a phase coupled to both modulus and divisor index.", "tests": "Mellin inversion, Cauchy–Schwarz, row variance and common-divisor CRT marginals.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md", "novelty_claim": false, "provenance_file": "connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl"}','A Mellin representation isolates a genuine moving additive phase. Abstract row-wise progression norms do not control it without further structure.','connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-CSTAR-PADDED-WEIGHT-AND-FIXED-RESIDUE','connections/connections.jsonl',72,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md','{"id": "CONN-CSTAR-PADDED-WEIGHT-AND-FIXED-RESIDUE", "sources": ["THM-PRIME-PRODUCT-EXACT-PADDED-FACTORABILITY", "OPEN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-MOVING-PHASE-SQUARE"], "statement": "The complete prime-product coefficient meets a padded factorability condition in the longest-block range. The phase target needs simultaneous varying residues.", "hypotheses": "Full normalized prime-product coefficient and Pascadi''s fixed-residue setting at the padded level.", "already_proved": "Exact minimal level and the longest-block exponent comparison.", "conjectural": "Control of the signed moving phase with the genuinely supported moduli.", "next_step": "Look for arithmetic inputs that retain the residue Fourier mode.", "source_theorems": ["THM-PRIME-PRODUCT-EXACT-PADDED-FACTORABILITY", "OPEN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-MOVING-PHASE-SQUARE"], "source_claims": [{"id": "THM-PRIME-PRODUCT-EXACT-PADDED-FACTORABILITY", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md · Exact padded factorability"}, {"id": "OPEN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-MOVING-PHASE-SQUARE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md · The exact prime form"}, {"locator": "sources/prime117_references/pascadi.pdf · p. 2, Definition 1.1 and Theorem 1.3(i)"}], "compatible_assumptions": "Full normalized prime-product coefficient and Pascadi''s fixed-residue setting at the padded level.", "new_claim_suggested": "Control of the signed moving phase with the genuinely supported moduli.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Control of the signed moving phase with the genuinely supported moduli.", "next_precise_step": "Look for arithmetic inputs that retain the residue Fourier mode.", "potential_counterexamples": "An insufficient prescribed split excludes the top prime power. Neither hard dyadic restriction nor the moving residue phase is covered by the factorization proof.", "significance": "Settles the precise coefficient-level obstruction and locates the remaining phase restriction.", "difficulty": "Elementary for the exact factorability. High for an applicable signed phase estimate.", "tests": "Integer allocation over every split and a prescribed split excluding the top prime power.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md", "novelty_claim": false, "provenance_file": "connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl"}','The complete prime-product coefficient meets a padded factorability condition in the longest-block range. The phase target needs simultaneous varying residues.','connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-GONEK-FIORI-EXPLICIT-ABEL-INPUT','connections/connections.jsonl',73,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_explicit_abel_round15.md','{"id": "CONN-GONEK-FIORI-EXPLICIT-ABEL-INPUT", "sources": ["PAPER-P122-FIORI-JASKARI-PNT", "PAPER-LF63-GONEK1984", "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-ABEL-PRIME-SUBSTITUTION"], "statement": "The unconditional absolute PNT error gives a uniform explicit bound for the prime-to-integral step in Gonek Lemma 8.", "hypotheses": "Pinned versions with Stieltjes upper endpoint included and finite-interval complex-shift control.", "already_proved": "Explicit real and complex Abel bounds.", "conjectural": "Numerical constants for the rest of the weighted derivative-tail argument.", "next_step": "Allocate constants to the remaining divisor, contour and tail estimates.", "source_theorems": ["PAPER-P122-FIORI-JASKARI-PNT", "PAPER-LF63-GONEK1984", "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-ABEL-PRIME-SUBSTITUTION"], "source_claims": [{"id": "PAPER-P122-FIORI-JASKARI-PNT", "locator": "arXiv:2609.23222v2 · Theorem 1.1/table p. 4, Theorem 5.2 p. 44, §5.1 p. 45"}, {"id": "PAPER-LF63-GONEK1984", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_gonek_whole_round15.md · 1984 journal Lemma 8"}, {"id": "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-ABEL-PRIME-SUBSTITUTION", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_explicit_abel_round15.md · Uniform Abel estimate"}], "compatible_assumptions": "Pinned versions with Stieltjes upper endpoint included and finite-interval complex-shift control.", "new_claim_suggested": "Numerical constants for the rest of the weighted derivative-tail argument.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Numerical constants for the rest of the weighted derivative-tail argument.", "next_precise_step": "Allocate constants to the remaining divisor, contour and tail estimates.", "potential_counterexamples": "For negative imaginary shifts the factor u^(−Im δ) must be bounded on the finite interval before integrating the remaining error to infinity.", "significance": "Supplies an explicit constant for one reusable step in the derivative-moment proof.", "difficulty": "Direct for the Abel step. A full numerical onset requires separate divisor, contour and tail constants.", "tests": "Absolute error integration and two independent Stieltjes calculations.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_explicit_abel_round15.md", "novelty_claim": false, "provenance_file": "connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl"}','The unconditional absolute PNT error gives a uniform explicit bound for the prime-to-integral step in Gonek Lemma 8.','connections/research_round15_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-MELLIN-SIGNED-LOCAL-REGULARITY','connections/connections.jsonl',74,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md','{"id": "CONN-MELLIN-SIGNED-LOCAL-REGULARITY", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md", "source_theorems": ["EXT-TITCH-1986-9.6A", "PAPER-M001", "THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-STRIP-SYMMETRIC-EXPLICIT-FORMULA", "LEM-MELLIN-SELBERG-PROJECTION-AND-COUNT-REMAINDER", "THM-MELLIN-LOG-SIGNED-HALF-AXIS-CONVERGENCE", "LEM-BL-LITERAL-TEST-CLASS-LOCAL-MELLIN-H1", "OBS-MELLIN-LOG-SIGNED-BOUNDARY-CUSP", "OBS-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ENDPOINT-ABSOLUTE-DIVERGENCE"], "source_claims": [{"id": "EXT-TITCH-1986-9.6A", "locator": "Titchmarsh–Heath-Brown, second ed. (1986), Chapter IX, Theorem 9.6(A), printed p. 217"}, {"id": "PAPER-M001", "locator": "Titchmarsh–Heath-Brown, second ed. (1986), Chapter IX, Theorem 9.19(C), printed p. 237"}, {"id": "PAPER-M001", "locator": "Titchmarsh–Heath-Brown, second ed. (1986), Chapter IX, Notes §9.25 (9.25.1), with Theorem 9.3"}, {"id": "THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-STRIP-SYMMETRIC-EXPLICIT-FORMULA", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md"}, {"id": "LEM-MELLIN-SELBERG-PROJECTION-AND-COUNT-REMAINDER", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md"}, {"id": "THM-MELLIN-LOG-SIGNED-HALF-AXIS-CONVERGENCE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md"}, {"id": "LEM-BL-LITERAL-TEST-CLASS-LOCAL-MELLIN-H1", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md"}, {"id": "OBS-MELLIN-LOG-SIGNED-BOUNDARY-CUSP", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md"}, {"id": "OBS-MELLIN-CRITICAL-LOG-ENDPOINT-ABSOLUTE-DIVERGENCE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_critical_endpoint_round15.md"}], "statement": "Sharp Fourier inversion on the two exterior lines gives the critical symmetric formula. The independent Selberg projection method gives separate half-axis convergence for p>1.", "compatible_assumptions": "Finite critical Mellin strip norm, original endpoint value bounds, and local H¹ in log coordinates for the contour theorem. Literal (A) and the norm imply the local condition. The Selberg route imposes the stronger p>1 weight.", "already_proved": "Ordinary inclusive symmetric convergence at p=0 including the smooth p=3 absolute-divergence witness, separate convergence on each half-axis for p>1, and signed failure for a continuous cusp outside the local and literal source classes.", "new_claim_suggested": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "potential_counterexamples": "The compact p=3 cusp defeats the norm and value hypotheses alone, with divergent local archimedean integral.", "significance": "Separates critical signed symmetric convergence with local regularity from the p>3 universal absolute trace. Luecking''s Bergman embedding is context for the ambient absolute threshold only.", "difficulty": "Uses endpoint Fourier inversion and a good-height contour, with additional work needed for weaker strip or local conditions.", "next_precise_step": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "tests": "Sharp versus Gaussian inversion, folded ξ′/ξ contour, restoration of exact heights, Selberg estimates, and compact smooth approximation.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "novelty_claim": false, "context_sources": [{"id": "PAPER-LUECKING1986-BERGMAN-MULTIPLIERS", "locator": "sources/prime146_mellin_provenance/luecking1986.pdf · p. 126, Bergman embedding theorem, and p. 127, radius lemma", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/prime146_mellin_trace_prior_art.md", "scope": "Ambient absolute-sampling threshold only; no signed raw-height implication."}], "provenance_file": "connections/research_round16_connections.jsonl", "original_status": "adjudicated_scoped", "conjectural": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "next_step": "Investigate weaker local assumptions and separate half-axis convergence for 0≤p≤1.", "latest_signed_log_boundary": "Round 17 closes the weaker logarithmic-weight question for universal ordinary symmetric summation in the stated class. The critical weight suffices and one smooth witness defeats every strict weakening. Weaker local conditions and the separate half-axis threshold remain independent.", "latest_signed_log_claim_ids": ["LEM-MELLIN-NEGATIVE-LOG-SHARP-INVERSION-PACKET", "OBS-MELLIN-ALL-NEGATIVE-LOG-SIGNED-DIVERGENCE", "THM-MELLIN-EXACT-SIGNED-LOG-BOUNDARY"], "status_update_evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_negative_mellin_round17.md"}','Sharp Fourier inversion on the two exterior lines gives the critical symmetric formula. The independent Selberg projection method gives separate half-axis convergence for p>1.','connections/research_round16_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-GONEK-EXPLICIT-CONVOLUTION-AND-ABEL','connections/connections.jsonl',75,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_gonek_constants_round16.md','{"id": "CONN-GONEK-EXPLICIT-CONVOLUTION-AND-ABEL", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_gonek_constants_round16.md", "source_theorems": ["PAPER-LF63-GONEK1984", "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-POSITIVE-DERIVATIVE-CONVOLUTION", "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-LEMMA8-ORDER-ONE-PAIR", "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-ABEL-PRIME-SUBSTITUTION"], "source_claims": [{"id": "PAPER-LF63-GONEK1984", "locator": "1984 journal pp. 133–135, Lemmas 7–8"}, {"id": "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-POSITIVE-DERIVATIVE-CONVOLUTION", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_gonek_constants_round16.md"}, {"id": "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-LEMMA8-ORDER-ONE-PAIR", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_gonek_constants_round16.md"}, {"id": "LEM-GONEK-EXPLICIT-ABEL-PRIME-SUBSTITUTION", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_explicit_abel_round15.md"}], "statement": "An explicit positive-order divisor estimate combines with the Abel prime substitution to bound the finite (1,1) step in Lemma 8.", "compatible_assumptions": "Positive integer derivative orders in the convolution and real shifts |δ|≤1/2 in the finite (1,1) application.", "already_proved": "An all-positive-order convolution constant and an explicit bound for the combined (1,1) finite remainder.", "new_claim_suggested": "Allocate constants in the remaining steps to obtain a certified onset for the derivative-tail estimate.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Allocate constants in the remaining steps to obtain a certified onset for the derivative-tail estimate.", "potential_counterexamples": "The two-positive-order floor centering argument relies on vanishing weights at both endpoints. A zero order needs its own boundary analysis.", "significance": "Quantifies two reusable arithmetic steps in a numerical derivative-tail argument.", "difficulty": "Elementary for the finite estimates. A full onset requires additional contour and tail analysis.", "next_precise_step": "Bound the derivative gamma factors and associated contour errors with verified constants.", "tests": "Right-continuous floor summation, unimodality, a beta integral and the independently bounded Abel error.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "novelty_claim": false, "provenance_file": "connections/research_round16_connections.jsonl"}','An explicit positive-order divisor estimate combines with the Abel prime substitution to bound the finite (1,1) step in Lemma 8.','connections/research_round16_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-MELLIN-CRITICAL-SIGNED-SHARP-LOG-BOUNDARY','connections/connections.jsonl',76,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_negative_mellin_round17.md','{"id": "CONN-MELLIN-CRITICAL-SIGNED-SHARP-LOG-BOUNDARY", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_negative_mellin_round17.md", "source_theorems": ["THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-STRIP-SYMMETRIC-EXPLICIT-FORMULA", "LEM-BL-LITERAL-TEST-CLASS-LOCAL-MELLIN-H1", "LEM-MELLIN-NEGATIVE-LOG-SHARP-INVERSION-PACKET", "OBS-MELLIN-ALL-NEGATIVE-LOG-SIGNED-DIVERGENCE", "THM-MELLIN-EXACT-SIGNED-LOG-BOUNDARY"], "source_claims": [{"id": "THM-MELLIN-CRITICAL-STRIP-SYMMETRIC-EXPLICIT-FORMULA", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md · Endpoint sharp Fourier inversion"}, {"id": "LEM-BL-LITERAL-TEST-CLASS-LOCAL-MELLIN-H1", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_signed_mellin_round16.md · Literal local hypotheses"}, {"id": "LEM-MELLIN-NEGATIVE-LOG-SHARP-INVERSION-PACKET", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_negative_mellin_round17.md · One packet"}, {"id": "OBS-MELLIN-ALL-NEGATIVE-LOG-SIGNED-DIVERGENCE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_negative_mellin_round17.md · A single globally smooth test"}, {"id": "THM-MELLIN-EXACT-SIGNED-LOG-BOUNDARY", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_negative_mellin_round17.md · What this obstruction says"}], "statement": "The critical strip norm gives uniform sharp inversion needed for the full prime sum. Every strict logarithmic weakening admits one escaped-center smooth witness defeating the symmetric formula.", "compatible_assumptions": "Fixed positive strip margin, original value envelopes and local H¹ or literal manuscript (A) for the positive theorem. The smooth witness satisfies literal (A) and (B) on any fixed 0<ε<1/4.", "already_proved": "Critical sufficiency, per-stage packet gain, and one witness with all negative-log norms finite, zero prime samples, finite arithmetic terms and two incompatible subsequences.", "new_claim_suggested": "Determine whether a trace formula with a different infinite atomic input admits the same exact logarithmic boundary.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Determine whether a trace formula with a different infinite atomic input admits the same exact logarithmic boundary.", "potential_counterexamples": "Pointwise inversion at each fixed prime-power argument can hold while the infinite weighted prime sum fails to converge under the contour cutoff.", "significance": "Closes the universal signed symmetric boundary problem raised in Round 16 within the stated norm scale.", "difficulty": "The one-witness statement requires stage-specific norm and finite-height budgets in addition to the fixed-prime packet estimate.", "next_precise_step": "Specify one other arithmetic trace formula and check its contour bounds and atomic coefficients before transferring the construction.", "tests": "Tilted interpolation, the sharp Dirichlet kernel, good-height contour, and diagonal control of two subsequences.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "novelty_claim": false, "provenance_file": "connections/research_round17_connections.jsonl"}','The critical strip norm gives uniform sharp inversion needed for the full prime sum. Every strict logarithmic weakening admits one escaped-center smooth witness defeating the symmetric formula.','connections/research_round17_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-CSTAR-COMMON-SEQUENCE-NORM-OBSTRUCTION','connections/connections.jsonl',77,'adjudicated_scoped','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_common_sequence_round17.md','{"id": "CONN-CSTAR-COMMON-SEQUENCE-NORM-OBSTRUCTION", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_common_sequence_round17.md", "source_theorems": ["OBS-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-PROGRESSION-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "OPEN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-MOVING-PHASE-SQUARE", "OBS-CSTAR-COMMON-NONNEGATIVE-SEQUENCE-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "OBS-CSTAR-COMMON-INTEGER-SEQUENCE-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "OBS-CSTAR-BOUNDED-COMMON-REAL-SEQUENCE-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "OBS-CSTAR-BOUNDED-COMMON-INTEGER-SEQUENCE-NORM-COUNTERMODEL"], "source_claims": [{"id": "OBS-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-PROGRESSION-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md · An exact limitation of two progression norms"}, {"id": "OPEN-CSTAR-LONG-PRIME-MOVING-PHASE-SQUARE", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_long_prime_round15.md · The exact prime form"}, {"id": "OBS-CSTAR-COMMON-NONNEGATIVE-SEQUENCE-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_common_sequence_round17.md · Exact statement"}, {"id": "OBS-CSTAR-COMMON-INTEGER-SEQUENCE-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_common_sequence_round17.md · Integer-valued realization with exact mass"}, {"id": "OBS-CSTAR-BOUNDED-COMMON-REAL-SEQUENCE-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_bounded_common_checkpoint14.md · Bounded construction and progression budgets"}, {"id": "OBS-CSTAR-BOUNDED-COMMON-INTEGER-SEQUENCE-NORM-COUNTERMODEL", "locator": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_bounded_common_checkpoint14.md · Cap-preserving integerization"}], "statement": "Common-sequence consistency, exact mass and uniform pointwise caps allow the large h=1 phase projection under P/k and induced-unit-mean discrepancy budgets.", "compatible_assumptions": "One ordinary integer interval, exact mass P, all-residue or induced-unit centering and the h=1 phase over the full narrow-band fourth-power support.", "already_proved": "Nonnegative real and integer versions with exact mass, stated two norm budgets, common-divisor compatibility and the phase lower bound. The bounded versions have real weights in [1/2,3/2] or integer weights in {0,1,2} on J. The unit-centered real projection against W(n)=Σ_(k∈S)(c_k/k)·1_((n,k)=1)·(cos(2πn/k)−μ(k)/φ(k)) is ≫|S|√T, exceeding T log⁴T by a divergent factor.", "new_claim_suggested": "Determine what additional sieve or prime-support structure controls the genuine moving phase.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Determine what additional sieve or prime-support structure controls the genuine moving phase.", "potential_counterexamples": "The example allows mass on nonunits. Its stated bounds compare with P/k or an induced unit mean, and give no corresponding bound about the prime-model P/φ(k).", "significance": "Strengthens the earlier abstract row obstruction while preserving the open arithmetic estimate.", "difficulty": "Finite Fourier and sampling estimates suffice for the abstract examples. Sieve support or the genuine prime phase needs separate estimates.", "next_precise_step": "Test centered norm inequalities with the actual prime-model unit baseline or explicit sieve weights.", "tests": "Short positive convolution, rational-frequency Gram bounds, imprimitive denominator accounting and multinomial sampling. The bounded versions use the second-derivative estimate for the full modulus shell, the positive selected-frequency diagonal, and bounded rounding with a single-unit mass correction.", "status": "adjudicated_scoped", "novelty_claim": false, "provenance_file": "connections/research_round17_connections.jsonl", "original_status": "adjudicated_scoped", "status_update_evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_bounded_common_checkpoint14.md"}','Common-sequence consistency, exact mass and uniform pointwise caps allow the large h=1 phase projection under P/k and induced-unit-mean discrepancy budgets.','connections/research_round17_connections.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-R001','connections/connections.jsonl',78,'scoped independently checked; director adjudicated','audits/adversarial_reviews/af_boundary_repair.md','{"id": "CONN-R001", "source_theorems": ["PAPER-A004:Proposition5.2", "THM-R002-FRAME"], "statement": "A sampled Fourier-family frame bound plus exterior squared tails supplies a replacement estimate for a normalized explicit-formula matrix truncation.", "compatible_assumptions": "Same fixed smooth window, Fourier convention,grid2pi/L, weight envelope and a>c as source.", "already_proved": "Unweighted Gram<=2piL I, weighted Gram O(BL), exterior mass O(BLlogL); E2 O(B²L²logL).", "conjectural_part": "Extension to weaker local weight assumptions and other explicit-formula matrices.", "next_step": "Derive weighted frame embedding under local L² control and test spike counterexamples.", "potential_counterexamples": "Dropping decay or uniform derivative norms can destroy integrability/scaling; no global boundedness of nu is assumed.", "tests": "Analytic proof plus three independent reconstructions; no numeric proof claim.", "significance": "Reusable alternate truncation proof; full source theorem not certified.", "difficulty": "elementary/moderate current lemma; high for arithmetic extensions", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/af_boundary_repair.md", "verification": "scoped independently checked; director adjudicated", "provenance_file": "connections/root_track.jsonl"}','A sampled Fourier-family frame bound plus exterior squared tails supplies a replacement estimate for a normalized explicit-formula matrix truncation.','connections/root_track.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-R002','connections/connections.jsonl',79,'scoped independently checked; director adjudicated','proposals/independent_campaigns/li_advocate.md','{"id": "CONN-R002", "source_theorems": ["PAPER-L002:Theorem1 and Corollary1", "THM-L001", "THM-L002"], "statement": "General Li multiset criterion has an essential every-index quantifier that cannot be replaced by a finite prefix using only symmetry,orderone and smooth zero-count main terms.", "compatible_assumptions": "Real symmetric entire products,normalized nonzero at0,1,zeros in criticalstrip; paired product convergence. No arithmetic axioms.", "already_proved": "Explicit planted quartets preserve every prescribed finite positive prefix, including counting-matched baseline.", "conjectural_part": "Whether any effective additional arithmetic tail criterion suffices.", "next_step": "State exact arithmetic tail hypothesis and identify the step excluding quartet construction.", "potential_counterexamples": "Counting-matched off-line quartet is explicit negative control.", "tests": "Exact rational quartet witness and analytic baseline bound; highprecision sums supplementary only.", "significance": "Prevents generic finite-certificate overclaims; no RH theorem.", "difficulty": "elementary model; arithmetic task extremely high", "evidence": "proposals/independent_campaigns/li_advocate.md", "verification": "scoped independently checked; director adjudicated", "provenance_file": "connections/root_track.jsonl"}','General Li multiset criterion has an essential every-index quantifier that cannot be replaced by a finite prefix using only symmetry,orderone and smooth zero-count main terms.','connections/root_track.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-RST048-ARITHMETIC','connections/connections.jsonl',80,'adjudicated_scoped_source_connection; extension_speculative','audits/adversarial_reviews/director_rstation48_main_theorem_round6.md; cited independent reviews; exactv2sourcehash','{"id": "CONN-RST048-ARITHMETIC", "source_theorems": ["THM-RST048-OPTIMAL", "LEM-RST048-CLUSTER", "LEM-RST048-INTEGER", "LEM-RST048-LOCAL-REPAIR"], "statement": "The source adaptive contour/profile construction supplies an actual arithmetic upper approximant where the Observatory''s earlier fixed-cluster polynomial Gram route stopped at an unproved growing-cluster transfer.", "compatible_assumptions": "RH aligns all roots; arbitrary complex integer Dirichlet coefficients of length<=N; full Cauchy boundary norm; fixed tiny contour mesh; multiplicities unrestricted and no growing inverse Gram matrix. This is an alternative proof route, not a claim that the earlier missing Gram lemma now follows.", "new_claim_suggested": "Investigate a fixed-degree L-function analog only after explicitly verifying small-window counts, reciprocal contours, Dirichlet synthesis and its pole/anchor structure.", "already_proved": "Source Theorem1 scoped reconstruction and fixed-Laurent qualification; published Burnol lower bound matches integer cutoff exactly. Source credit retained.", "conjectural_or_unresolved": "Effective finite-N constants, independent external expert assessment, exact publication priority, prefix lower bound and finite-off-line extensions; transfer beyond zeta not proved.", "next_precise_step": "Quantify the finite-Y local error and tail under explicit certified reciprocal bounds; independently reconstruct compact-jet prefix lower bound from paper47.", "potential_counterexamples": "Off-line poles destroy unit-modulus convolution phases. Pole data alone can hide an entire remainder. Summability of individual norms is neither implied nor needed. A continuous correction without quadrature need not lie in zeta D_N.", "tests": "Independent full main-proof reconstructions, exact norm/cutoff check against Burnol, termwise local repair, rational cutoff exponent and profile controls; infinite assertions rest on analytic proofs.", "significance": "Supports an RH-only optimized rate in a primary manuscript with fewer hypotheses than the inspected BCF prescribed-array theorem; no independent publication or discovery claim.", "difficulty": "Substantial analytic contour, growing multiplicity and arithmetic approximation argument.", "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_rstation48_main_theorem_round6.md; cited independent reviews; exactv2sourcehash", "status": "adjudicated_scoped_source_connection; extension_speculative", "provenance_file": "connections/rstation48_director_round6.jsonl"}','The source adaptive contour/profile construction supplies an actual arithmetic upper approximant where the Observatory''s earlier fixed-cluster polynomial Gram route stopped at an unproved growing-cluster transfer.','connections/rstation48_director_round6.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-E-W301','connections/connections.jsonl',81,'independently_checked_finite_lemma_and_asymptotic','proposals/independent_campaigns/unit_circle_scalar_window_round3.md','{"id": "CONN-E-W301", "source_papers": ["PAPER-E002", "PAPER-E010"], "source_theorems": ["THM-E003", "THM-E-W301", "THM-E-W303"], "source_locators": ["BurnolTheorem1.4; all-root unit-circle restriction", "Beneteauet al2015Thm3.4 internalpp16–17"], "claim": "A degree-m scalar taper applied directly to reciprocal coefficients is collision-uniform and attains the known optimal coalescent leading multiplicity² constant without separation assumptions.", "compatible_assumptions": "Fixed finite degree,multiplicities allowed, standard H² coefficient norm; do not import norm-dependent exact formulas from equivalent Dirichlet-type norms.", "established_part": ["Collision-uniform K_m/M bound", "Complete coalescence m²/M+O_m(M^-2)"], "conjectural_part": "General coalescence-maximum statement for arbitrary m,M; no arithmetic transfer.", "next_step": "Prove or refute global root-configuration maximum, or derive sharper fixed-m constants through a valid symmetric gap decomposition.", "counterexample_risks": ["Raw Laurent coefficients already negative for m3M2; coefficientwise positivity proof fails.", "Constants dependm; growing-degree inference unsupported."], "tests": ["Exact rational unit_circle_scalar_window_round3.py", "Exact negative Laurent witness scalar_window_laurent_round3.py"], "evidence": "proposals/independent_campaigns/unit_circle_scalar_window_round3.md", "verification": "independently_checked_finite_lemma_and_asymptotic", "novelty": "unassessed_not_claimed", "provenance_file": "connections/scalar_window_round3.jsonl"}','A degree-m scalar taper applied directly to reciprocal coefficients is collision-uniform and attains the known optimal coalescent leading multiplicity² constant without separation assumptions.','connections/scalar_window_round3.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-E-W302','connections/connections.jsonl',82,'arithmetic_extension_pending_independent_review','proposals/independent_campaigns/logarithmic_riesz_multiplicity_round3.md§§1–5','{"id": "CONN-E-W302", "source_papers": ["PAPER-C105", "PAPER-E011", "PAPER-M002"], "source_theorems": ["THM-E-W307", "THM-E-W308", "THM-E-W310"], "source_locators": ["Wei–Wu2022Prop1.9 and proof targeted prior q1alpha1", "Inouev2Theorem1p3,Lemma6pp13–14", "Hardy–Riesz1915pp21–23,50–51"], "claim": "Finite reciprocal-polynomial convergence threshold p>m−1 exactly matches the necessary logarithmic Möbius-window multiplicity inequality alpha>m−1. Changing fixed spectral q preserves the arithmetic scalar coefficient witness.", "verified_compatible_assumptions": "Compare the same fixed window order and zero multiplicity; polynomial result is sufficient+necessary within its finite model, arithmetic result only necessary and requires full-sequence norm convergence. Fixed integer q>=1.", "established_part": "Finite model threshold checked by power-sum/terminal method; arithmetic extension explicitly derived but independent review pending.", "conjectural_part": "Any arithmetic sufficiency or summability across infinitely many zeros; not supplied by finite match.", "next_step": "Independently review fractional cutoff interpolation and quantitative Gamma coefficient, then identify a real Möbius cancellation estimate sufficient for prescribed-window convergence.", "counterexample_risks": ["Sparse N subsequences do not supply full real-x little-o bound for boundary multiplicity.", "Logarithmic and arithmetic Riesz orders cannot be identified.", "Numerical agreement or finite interpolation cannot control zero-height tails."], "tests": "Symbolic Mellin and Abelian proof; no numerical evidence substituted for proof.", "evidence": "proposals/independent_campaigns/logarithmic_riesz_multiplicity_round3.md§§1–5", "verification": "arithmetic_extension_pending_independent_review", "novelty": "classical_pole_mechanism; no_priority_claim", "provenance_file": "connections/scalar_window_round3.jsonl"}','Finite reciprocal-polynomial convergence threshold p>m−1 exactly matches the necessary logarithmic Möbius-window multiplicity inequality alpha>m−1. Changing fixed spectral q preserves the arithmetic scalar coefficient witness.','connections/scalar_window_round3.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-E-W303','connections/connections.jsonl',83,'targeted_primary_source_checked','papers/PAPER-M002.md;papers/PAPER-E011.md','{"id": "CONN-E-W303", "source_papers": ["PAPER-M002", "PAPER-E011"], "source_theorems": ["THM-E-W309"], "source_locators": ["Hardy–RieszTheorem39p50,Eq2p51;Theorem40p51", "InoueEq3.1–3.2pp13–14"], "claim": "The first-kind logarithmic Mellin kernel Gamma(alpha+1)/(s^(alpha+1)zeta(s)) and second-kind arithmetic kernel Gamma(s)/(Gamma(1+tau+s)zeta(s)) both retain nonzero critical-zero pole coefficients but have different smoothing dependence.", "verified_compatible_assumptions": "Positive fixed real orders; absolutely convergent initial Mellin integrals; nontrivial zero rho has nonzero imaginary part so Gamma factors finite/nonzero.", "established_part": "Classical mean definitions and distinct kernels directly checked against primary source; Abelian method usable after the appropriate growth bound.", "conjectural_part": "No automatic quantitative uniformity as order varies.", "next_step": "Track growing-order Gamma and reciprocal-zeta estimates before any contour shift.", "counterexample_risks": ["A mistaken identification of tau withalpha changes the residue and may invent a multiplicity ceiling."], "tests": "Primary visual equation comparison and exact Mellin interchange.", "evidence": "papers/PAPER-M002.md;papers/PAPER-E011.md", "verification": "targeted_primary_source_checked", "novelty": "historical_dictionary_not_new_theorem", "provenance_file": "connections/scalar_window_round3.jsonl"}','The first-kind logarithmic Mellin kernel Gamma(alpha+1)/(s^(alpha+1)zeta(s)) and second-kind arithmetic kernel Gamma(s)/(Gamma(1+tau+s)zeta(s)) both retain nonzero critical-zero pole coefficients but have different smoothing dependence.','connections/scalar_window_round3.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "connections" VALUES('CONN-E-W304','connections/connections.jsonl',84,'original_contour_established; growing_order_convergence_proposed_pending_independent_review','proposals/independent_campaigns/logarithmic_riesz_multiplicity_round3.md§6','{"id": "CONN-E-W304", "source_papers": ["PAPER-E001", "PAPER-M001", "PAPER-M002"], "source_theorems": ["THM-E-W309"], "source_locators": ["AuditedBaez-Duarteuniformdependency reconstruction", "Hardy–RieszTheorem39p50"], "claim": "For alpha_N=epsilon_N logN growing and epsilon_N decreasing, the logarithmic Perron saddle lies near epsilon_N and suggests approximation of1/zeta(s+epsilon_N), but the needed weighted critical-line saddle/tail estimate is unproved.", "compatible_assumptions": "epsilon_N>0,epsilon_N->0,epsilon_N logN->infty; fixed q>=1; prospective RH-conditional analysis; initial contour lies right of absolute convergence.", "established_part": "Exact initial-line contour and restricted pointwise logarithmic-weight expansion.", "conjectural_part": "Integral_R |zeta(s)|²|V_N,alpha_N(s)−1/zeta(s+epsilon_N)|²/|s|^(2q)dt->0 at s=.5+it.", "next_step": "Bound inverse-zeta derivatives, critical-zero neighborhoods, contour tails and the full weighted height integral uniformly, starting with epsilon_N=c/loglogN.", "counterexample_risks": ["Pointwise coefficient approximation fails near n=N and does not imply norm convergence.", "Moving order invalidates fixed-order implicit constants.", "Saddle expansion alone does not bound a full critical-line integral."], "tests": "Prove explicit weighted error estimate; numerical quadrature would be supplementary only.", "evidence": "proposals/independent_campaigns/logarithmic_riesz_multiplicity_round3.md§6", "verification": "original_contour_established; growing_order_convergence_proposed_pending_independent_review", "novelty": "unassessed_not_claimed", "followup_claim": "THM-E-W312 now supplies a complete RH-conditional proof attempt using a complex Perron approximate identity