3, Theorems 12 and 14, article pp. 10–16", "scoped_statement": "Relates balanced Nyman–Beurling floor sums to integral factorial ratios. Theorem 14 uses the equivalent n⁻² sequence norm and the kernel n^(−ρ)−(n+1)^(−ρ) to obstruct approximation of the constant at a right-hand zero.", "selection_reason": "Exact primary antecedent joining the central factorial family, balanced floor functions, and a sequence-space zeta-zero witness.", "bibliographic_verified": true, "access_date": "2026-11-17", "full_text_accessed": true, "whole_work_read": false, "substantive_reading": false, "audit_level": 0, "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "record_path": "papers/density63_generator_antecedents.md", "audit_path": "audits/adversarial_reviews/jump_generator63_antecedents.md", "source_hash_manifest": "sources/jump_generator63_antecedents/SHA256SUMS", "novelty_claim": false, "id": "PAPER-GEN63-BORISOV", "arxiv": "math/0505167", "read_scope": "Targeted §3 opening on the central factorial ratio and balanced Nyman–Beurling floor sums, and proof passages in Theorem 14 using the eta identity and summation-by-parts zero witness. Singularity classification and remaining proofs were outside scope.", "original_access_status": "full_primary_text_accessed_targeted_portions_read", "track_file": "papers/density63_generator_antecedents_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": null, "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-GEN63-BORISOV"]}','Quotient Singularities, Integer Ratios of Factorials, and the Riemann Hypothesis','["Alexander Borisov"]',NULL,'2008',0,0,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','Published journal PDF, author-hosted copy','https://people.math.binghamton.edu/borisov/documents/papers/quot-fact-rh.pdf','33ca560d7c0a6a5de0cfad5508120b4152e36b96349cdd10372044e3ade41536','papers/density63_generator_antecedents.md','papers/density63_generator_antecedents_records.jsonl');
