quence, with distinct numbering and pagination. Direct bdim PDF download returned HTTP 503. The indexed journal scan displayed Lemma 1 and equation (2.1) on p. 6.", "version_history": "The v2 arXiv comment reports three typographical corrections and one added reference.", "related_sequel": "PAPER-E001 (arXiv:math/0205003), a separate work", "family": ["C", "A"], "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "full_text_accessed": true, "whole_work_read": false, "audit_level": 0, "read_scope": "Partial close reading of §§1–3 of arXiv v2, covering the main criterion, the quoted Möbius estimate, the quotient estimate and the ordered norm limits. Journal Lemma 1 was located independently in the indexed scan.", "source_path": "sources/ratio62_weightedprior/baez_duarte_0202141v2.pdf", "source_file": "sources/ratio62_weightedprior/baez_duarte_0202141v2.pdf", "source_sha256": "3ce4aff466443c71094affc1f8b6f5f0dd36cb4377dc5d2ceddbd2537c1d1819", "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "record_path": "papers/PAPER-E014.md", "audit_file": "audits/weighted_criterion_priority_ratio62.md", "main_result": "Theorem 1.1 in arXiv v2, and Theorem 1 on journal p. 5. RH is equivalent to the indicator of (0,1] lying in the closed L²(0,∞) span of the fractional parts {1/(nx)} for positive integers n.", "reusable_lemma": "ArXiv v2 Lemma 2.1, p. 3, equation (2.1), and journal Lemma 1, p. 6, equation (2.1), reproduce the fixed-gap Möbius approximation of PAPER-E007, Lemme 2, for any zero-free half-plane Re(s)>b, 1/2≤b<1.", "selected": true, "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "selection_reason": "Original source for the discrete Báez-Duarte criterion and a verified formula-complete quotation of the Balazard–Saias lemma used in the corrected weighted criterion.", "original_paper_id": "PAPER-E014", "work_id": "PAPER-E014", "manifestation_role": "February revision, with original record preserved"}, {"id": "PAPER-E001", "title": "A strengthening of the Nyman-Beurling criterion for the Riemann hypothesis, 2", "authors": ["Luis Báez-Duarte"], "date": "2002-05-01", "year": 2002, "doi": null, "arxiv": "math/0205003", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0205003v1", "version": "v1", "family": ["C", "A"], "audit_level": 1, "read_scope": "Complete nine-page preprint text read; ordered-limit argument reconstructed; external dependencies not fully independently checked.", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "venue": "arXiv preprint; distinct from original math/0202141 and subsequent published text", "publication_status": "preprint_version_inspected", "source_file": "baez_duarte", "main_result": "In H=L²((0,infinity),dx), let rho_a(x)={1/(a x)}, chi=1_(0,1], and B_nat=span{rho_a:a in positive integers}. RH iff chi belongs to the H closure of B_nat (Theorem1.1, pp.1–2). Under RH, for some c>0, ||chi+sum_{a<=n}mu(a)exp(-c log(a)/loglog(n))rho_a||_H << (loglog(n))^(-1/3) (Proposition3.1, pp.6–8).", "proof_architecture": ["RH plus Balazard–Saias truncated Möbius estimate", "Mellin transform of fractional part is -zeta(s)/s in 0<Re(s)<1", "Functional-equation ratio bound Lemma2.2", "H convergence n→infinity for fixed sufficiently small epsilon", "H convergence epsilon↓0 to -chi, then closure"], "limitations": ["No RH-independent construction attaining convergence is supplied.", "The two limits are ordered; pointwise convergence of raw Möbius truncations does not imply H convergence.", "Proposition3.1 is a sketch with external input.", "Displayed integrability range in p.5 needs epsilon<1/4 for the particular majorant; sufficiently small epsilon suffices."], "historical_importance": "Reduces continuous dilation parameters to integer dilations; turns an abstract closure criterion into arithmetic approximation.", "reusable_lemma": "Lemma2.2 bounds |zeta(1/2-epsilon+it)/zeta(1/2+epsilon+it)| by C(1+|t|)^epsilon, for 0<=epsilon<=epsilon0<1/2, interpreted at removable common zeros; the functional equation supplies the modulus bound.", "research_questions": ["Can a quantitative uniform error bound replace the sequential limiting argument?", "Which smoothing schemes preserve norm convergence with a useful explicit rate?"], "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "original_notation": "See downloaded source; normalized notation in this record uses rho for a zero except rho_a in E001.", "source_sha256": "13a2dcc763d3fdd5b52afc87845c6d77c83764a56aab06f574a91ee43c8a152b", "correction_search_status": "arXiv history inspected; exhaustive later-correction search incomplete", "original_paper_id": "PAPER-E001", "work_id": "PAPER-E014", "manifestation_role": "Expanded May deposit; original Level 1 source record preserved", "source_path": "sources/equivalences/baez_duarte.pdf"}], "manifestation_records": [{"version": "arXiv:math/0202141v1, 15 February 2002", "arxiv": "math/0202141v1", "source_path": "sources/analytic74_baez/math_0202141v1.pdf", "source_sha256": "a0b876c54be79af5d1af53d181c6cd6fc94d94cc35d32b22697a97b15c99f589", "audit_level": 1, "whole_work_read": true, "read_scope": "Complete preprint compared by both whole-work reviewers. No quantitative theorem in this version."}, {"id": "PAPER-E014", "title": "A strengthening of the Nyman–Beurling criterion for the Riemann hypothesis", "authors": ["Luis Báez-Duarte"], "date": "2002-02-18", "year": 2002, "first_preprint_date": "2002-02-15", "preprint_year": 2002, "publication_year": 2003, "version": "v2 (2002-02-18), seven-page arXiv preprint", "arxiv": "math/0202141", "doi": "10.48550/arXiv.math/0202141", "doi_scope": "DataCite identifier for the arXiv preprint", "journal_doi": null, "venue": "Rendiconti Lincei, Series 9, 14(1) (2003), 5–11", "publication_status": "Original arXiv preprint inspected. Relation to the published journal article verified by title, author, main theorem and the precise Balazard–Saias estimate in the indexed journal scan.", "canonical_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0202141v2", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0202141v2", "journal_source_url": "https://www.bdim.eu/item?fmt=pdf&id=RLIN_2003_9_14_1_5_0", "journal_relation_scope": "Journal form adds a section on a constructive approximating sequence, with distinct numbering and pagination. Direct bdim PDF download returned HTTP 503. The indexed journal scan displayed Lemma 1 and equation (2.1) on p. 6.", "version_history": "The v2 arXiv comment reports three typographical corrections and one added reference.", "related_sequel": "PAPER-E001 (arXiv:math/0205003), a separate work", "family": ["C", "A"], "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "full_text_accessed": true, "whole_work_read": false, "audit_level": 0, "read_scope": "Partial close reading of §§1–3 of arXiv v2, covering the main criterion, the quoted Möbius estimate, the quotient estimate and the ordered norm limits. Journal Lemma 1 was located independently in the indexed scan.", "source_path": "sources/ratio62_weightedprior/baez_duarte_0202141v2.pdf", "source_file": "sources/ratio62_weightedprior/baez_duarte_0202141v2.pdf", "source_sha256": "3ce4aff466443c71094affc1f8b6f5f0dd36cb4377dc5d2ceddbd2537c1d1819", "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "record_path": "papers/PAPER-E014.md", "audit_file": "audits/weighted_criterion_priority_ratio62.md", "main_result": "Theorem 1.1 in arXiv v2, and Theorem 1 on journal p. 5. RH is equivalent to the indicator of (0,1] lying in the closed L²(0,∞) span of the fractional parts {1/(nx)} for positive integers n.", "reusable_lemma": "ArXiv v2 Lemma 2.1, p. 3, equation (2.1), and journal Lemma 1, p. 6, equation (2.1), reproduce the fixed-gap Möbius approximation of PAPER-E007, Lemme 2, for any zero-free half-plane Re(s)>b, 1/2≤b<1.", "selected": true, "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "selection_reason": "Original source for the discrete Báez-Duarte criterion and a verified formula-complete quotation of the Balazard–Saias lemma used in the corrected weighted criterion.", "original_paper_id": "PAPER-E014", "work_id": "PAPER-E014", "manifestation_role": "February revision, with original record preserved"}, {"id": "PAPER-E001", "title": "A strengthening of the Nyman-Beurling criterion for the Riemann hypothesis, 2", "authors": ["Luis Báez-Duarte"], "date": "2002-05-01", "year": 2002, "doi": null, "arxiv": "math/0205003", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0205003v1", "version": "v1", "family": ["C", "A"], "audit_level": 1, "read_scope": "Complete nine-page preprint text read; ordered-limit argument reconstructed; external dependencies not fully independently checked.", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "venue": "arXiv preprint; distinct from original math/0202141 and subsequent published text", "publication_status": "preprint_version_inspected", "source_file": "baez_duarte", "main_result": "In H=L²((0,infinity),dx), let rho_a(x)={1/(a x)}, chi=1_(0,1], and B_nat=span{rho_a:a in positive integers}. RH iff chi belongs to the H closure of B_nat (Theorem1.1, pp.1–2). Under RH, for some c>0, ||chi+sum_{a<=n}mu(a)exp(-c log(a)/loglog(n))rho_a||_H << (loglog(n))^(-1/3) (Proposition3.1, pp.6–8).", "proof_architecture": ["RH plus Balazard–Saias truncated Möbius estimate", "Mellin transform of fractional part is -zeta(s)/s in 0<Re(s)<1", "Functional-equation ratio bound Lemma2.2", "H convergence n→infinity for fixed sufficiently small epsilon", "H convergence epsilon↓0 to -chi, then closure"], "limitations": ["No RH-independent construction attaining convergence is supplied.", "The two limits are ordered; pointwise convergence of raw Möbius truncations does not imply H convergence.", "Proposition3.1 is a sketch with external input.", "Displayed integrability range in p.5 needs epsilon<1/4 for the particular majorant; sufficiently small epsilon suffices."], "historical_importance": "Reduces continuous dilation parameters to integer dilations; turns an abstract closure criterion into arithmetic approximation.", "reusable_lemma": "Lemma2.2 bounds |zeta(1/2-epsilon+it)/zeta(1/2+epsilon+it)| by C(1+|t|)^epsilon, for 0<=epsilon<=epsilon0<1/2, interpreted at removable common zeros; the functional equation supplies the modulus bound.", "research_questions": ["Can a quantitative uniform error bound replace the sequential limiting argument?", "Which smoothing schemes preserve norm convergence with a useful explicit rate?"], "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "original_notation": "See downloaded source; normalized notation in this record uses rho for a zero except rho_a in E001.", "source_sha256": "13a2dcc763d3fdd5b52afc87845c6d77c83764a56aab06f574a91ee43c8a152b", "correction_search_status": "arXiv history inspected; exhaustive later-correction search incomplete", "original_paper_id": "PAPER-E001", "work_id": "PAPER-E014", "manifestation_role": "Expanded May deposit; original Level 1 source record preserved", "source_path": "sources/equivalences/baez_duarte.pdf"}], "related_sequel": null, "related_deposit": "PAPER-E001 is a stable work alias for the expanded May preprint, not a separate selected work.", "main_result": "Journal Theorem 1 (p5, proof pp6–9): in H=L²(0,infinity), RH iff chi=1_(0,1] belongs to the closure of the span of rho_n(x)={1/(nx)} for every integer n≥1. Journal Theorem 2 (pp9–10), the same result as expanded May Proposition3.1: under RH, for some fixed c>0 the damped Möbius approximants with exponent c/loglog n have norm error O((loglog n)^(−1/3)).", "reusable_lemma": "Journal Lemma 2 (pp6–7), expanded May Lemma2.2 and February Lemma2.2 with a version-specific gamma typo: the symmetric zeta quotient has modulus at most C_(epsilon0)(1+|t|)^epsilon for 0≤epsilon≤epsilon0<1/2, by the functional equation and uniform Stirling, with removable common zero values.", "original_notation": "rho_a denotes fractional-part dilations, chi the target indicator, H the full-half-axis L2 space. Historical E001 identifies the expanded May deposit; theorem numbering remains manifestation-specific.", "audit_level": 3, "whole_work_read": true, "substantive_reading": true, "read_scope": "Complete pinned journal, seven article pages, independently reconstructed by two agents and director. The integer criterion, corollary and RH-conditional rate survive local normalization/range/tail repairs and the separately established shrinking-gap supplement. The May and February deposits retain distinct manifestations and original reading scopes.", "claim_verification_status": "Whole-work Level 3 for the exact journal manifestation; original printed hypotheses and repaired deductions are distinguished. No RH proof or new rate claimed.", "limitations": ["All positive integer dilations including 1 are required.", "Norm limits are ordered; unconditional analytic-kernel convergence does not identify the actual damped functions off RH.", "The particular printed majorant needs epsilon<1/4; a free subpower exponent proves the fixed weighted range epsilon<1/2.", "Uniform shrinking-gap constants require the reconstructed supplement; no practical onset or optimality claimed."], "journal_relation_scope": "The original 2003 journal incorporates the quantitative theorem of the expanded May deposit; the author confirms this preprint relation in a contemporary self-citation.", "version_history": "February v1/v2, expanded May deposit under a second arXiv ID, then 2003 journal. Exact hashes, dates and equation numbering preserved in quality/baez_manifestation_identity_round13.json.", "correction_history": "Journal fixes February gamma denominator and transform interval. Local Mellin normalization, particular majorant range, tail exponent and conditional-identification qualifications have existing finding handles. Bounded search found no separately verified corrigendum."}, "evidence": "audits/adversarial_reviews/director_baez_whole_round13.md", "track_file": "quality/zzzzzzzz_round13_source_scope_updates.jsonl"}], "substantive_reading": true, "journal_relation_scope": "The original 2003 journal incorporates the quantitative theorem of the expanded May deposit; the author confirms this preprint relation in a c