inding handles. Bounded search found no separately verified corrigendum."}','A strengthening of the Nyman–Beurling criterion for the Riemann hypothesis','["Luis Báez-Duarte"]','["C", "A"]','2003',3,1,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','2003 Lincei journal scan, pp. 5–11, with two BDIM front sheets','http://www.bdim.eu/item?fmt=pdf&id=RLIN_2003_9_14_1_5_0','9bfb3943ec8d7690d452b8ac7d50fb10614b4e814738dc091390e6ab4994f0b8','papers/PAPER-E014.md','papers/equivalence_records.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('PAPER-E002','corpus/bibliography.jsonl',440,'full_text_accessed','papers/PAPER-E002.md','{"id": "PAPER-E002", "title": "A lower bound in an approximation problem involving the zeros of the Riemann zeta function", "authors": ["Jean-François Burnol"], "date": "2001-03-20", "year": 2001, "doi": "10.1006/aima.2001.2066", "arxiv": "math/0103058", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0103058v2", "version": "v2", "family": ["C", "D", "F"], "audit_level": 1, "read_scope": "Complete 17 printed-page preprint read; polynomial jet-projection method reconstructed; zeta invariant-operator lemmas read but not independently rebuilt.", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "venue": "Advances in Mathematics 170 (2002), 56–70; inspected 2001 preprint", "publication_status": "published_work_preprint_inspected", "source_file": "burnol", "main_result": "For B_lambda=span{{theta/t}:lambda<=theta<=1} in L²((0,infinity),dt), D(lambda)=dist(chi,B_lambda), liminf_{lambda↓0}D(lambda)*sqrt(log(1/lambda)) >= sqrt(sum_rho m_rho²/|rho|²) (Theorem1.3 p.4; Theorem5.5 pp.15–16). Proof assumes RH, since its failure makes the left side infinite; rho are distinct nontrivial zeros under that assumption. Polynomial analogue Theorem1.4: Q of positive degree with all roots alpha on the unit circle, multiplicities m_alpha, and fixed target polynomial P gives lim N inf_deg A<=N ||P-QA||²=sum_alpha m_alpha²|P(alpha)|².", "proof_architecture": ["Finite-dimensional prediction error and jet evaluation Gram matrices (§2)", "Mellin invariant unitary phase operator V (§3)", "Boundary-limit Hilbert vectors Y_(s,k)^lambda and orthogonality to contracted zeta model (§4)", "Rescale by log(1/lambda)^(-k-1/2)", "Fixed finite set of zeros gives Cauchy Gram blocks, whose inverse top-left entries are m²", "Take lower bound for every finite zero set; then increase the finite set"], "limitations": ["A lower bound only; no upper bound or complete spectral construction follows.", "Fixed finite-set Gram limits do not justify a uniform infinite-set limit.", "The conjectural disappearance of the continuous quotient component is explicitly speculative.", "D(lambda) allows continuous dilation parameters; discrete Dirichlet-polynomial distance is at least as large at lambda=1/N."], "historical_importance": "Identifies multiplicity squared, not multiplicity, as the approximation obstruction; converts zero jets to asymptotic Gram blocks.", "reusable_lemma": "Theorem5.3: distinct fixed zeros have asymptotically vanishing cross Gram entries after scaling; same-zero derivative jets give 1/(k+l+1).", "research_questions": ["Obtain uniform Gram estimates when zero separations shrink with the cutoff.", "Control any orthogonal complement beyond the constructed zero jets before asserting a matching upper bound."], "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "original_notation": "See downloaded source; normalized notation in this record uses rho for a zero except rho_a in E001.", "source_sha256": "999f05d5045fd909c3fb985677c4e40459f2a8b1e8b7d932f34b35bdc52d6e7d", "correction_search_status": "arXiv history inspected; exhaustive later-correction search incomplete", "original_access_status": "full_text_accessed", "whole_work_read": true, "record_path": "papers/PAPER-E002.md", "track_file": "papers/equivalence_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": null, "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-E002"]}','A lower bound in an approximation problem involving the zeros of the Riemann zeta function','["Jean-François Burnol"]','["C", "D", "F"]','2001',1,1,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','v2','https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0103058v2','999f05d5045fd909c3fb985677c4e40459f2a8b1e8b7d932f34b35bdc52d6e7d','papers/PAPER-E002.md','papers/equivalence_records.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('PAPER-E003','corpus/bibliography.jsonl',441,'full_text_accessed','papers/PAPER-E003.md','{"id": "PAPER-E003", "title": "An optimal choice of Dirichlet polynomials for the Nyman-Beurling criterion", "authors": ["Sandro Bettin", "J. Brian Conrey", "David W. Farmer"], "date": "2012-11-22", "year": 2012, "doi": "10.1134/S0081543813030036", "arxiv": "1211.5191", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1211.5191v1", "version": "v1", "family": ["A", "C"], "audit_level": 1, "read_scope": "Complete nine-page preprint read; hypotheses and residue proof architecture extracted; central contour estimates inspected, not all independently verified.", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "venue": "Proceedings of the Steklov Institute of Mathematics, 2013; preprint version inspected", "publication_status": "published_work_preprint_inspected", "source_file": "bcf", "main_result": "Assume RH and sum_{|Im rho|<=T}|zeta''(rho)|^(-2)<<T^(3/2-delta) for some delta>0. For V_N(s)=sum_{n<=N}(1-log n/log N)mu(n)n^(-s), N>1, its squared weighted critical-line error (1/(2pi))integral_R |1-zeta(1/2+it)V_N(1/2+it)|² dt/(1/4+t²) is asymptotic to (2+gamma-log(4pi))/log N (Theorem1,p.2). Moment hypothesis forces simple zeros. Theorem2,p.3: analogous triangular reciprocal Taylor window is asymptotically optimal for polynomials with simple roots on/outside the circle, if boundary roots are present.", "proof_architecture": ["Perron representation of logarithmically weighted Möbius polynomial", "Residues at pole s, nontrivial zeros, and trivial zeros (Lemma2)", "Reciprocal derivative moment controls sums of zero residues (Lemma3)", "Shift norm contour off critical line", "Double pole residue supplies sum 1/|rho|² log N; remaining integrals are lower order"], "limitations": ["RH alone is not the theorem hypothesis.", "Inverse derivative moment excludes multiplicities.", "Infinite-zero residue tails require the additional moment estimate.", "No finite-N inequality of the form d_N²>=C/log N is proved.", "Polynomial theorem with no boundary roots should be read as o(1/N), rather than literal asymptotic equivalence to zero."], "historical_importance": "Under an explicit strong arithmetic hypothesis, a concrete logarithmic Möbius smoothing attains Burnol’s asymptotic lower constant.", "reusable_lemma": "Lemma3 pp.6–7 supplies a bound on the sum of zero-residue terms on Re(s)=1/2±epsilon using the negative derivative moment.", "research_questions": ["Can collective residue cancellation weaken the exponent 3/2-delta?", "Which estimates replace inverse simple derivatives for higher principal parts?"], "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "original_notation": "See downloaded source; normalized notation in this record uses rho for a zero except rho_a in E001.", "source_sha256": "10aec1235df42b351c55b77b4b207802e867219560cff14eaa7b43e0aa425468", "correction_search_status": "arXiv history inspected; exhaustive later-correction search incomplete", "original_access_status": "full_text_accessed", "whole_work_read": true, "record_path": "papers/PAPER-E003.md", "track_file": "papers/equivalence_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": null, "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-E003"]}','An optimal choice of Dirichlet polynomials for the Nyman-Beurling criterion','["Sandro Bettin", "J. Brian Conrey", "David W. Farmer"]','["A", "C"]','2012',1,1,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','v1','https://arxiv.org/abs/1211.5191v1','10aec1235df42b351c55b77b4b207802e867219560cff14eaa7b43e0aa425468','papers/PAPER-E003.md','papers/equivalence_records.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('PAPER-E004','corpus/bibliography.jsonl',442,'full_text_accessed','papers/PAPER-E004.md','{"id": "PAPER-E004", "title": "On certain Gram matrices and their associated series", "authors": ["Werner Ehm"], "date": "2024-05-13", "year": 2024, "doi": null, "arxiv": "2405.06349", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.06349v2", "version": "v2", "family": ["C", "F"], "audit_level": 0, "read_scope": "Partial inspection only: introduction p.1 and selected §8 passages; no substantive whole-work reading or proof audit claimed.", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "publication_status": "preprint_version_inspected", "source_sha256": "3cb69fccea75e07f768e6af5a74ca2ea4640414cbedb9b0875bb5510c8a2d288", "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "main_result": "Not extracted as a verified result; candidate source for exact Gram-kernel identities (Theorem2.1) and arithmetic quadratic-form decompositions (§8).", "limitations": ["The sentence after Proposition1.1 relating fixed Selberg coefficients to RH requires contextual literature verification; the necessary external convergence result has not been located in this track.", "No assertion of error or novelty.", "Theorem2.1 and subsequent proofs remain unread in full."], "next_step": "Check RH-alone norm convergence of the fixed Selberg sequence before evaluating the introductory equivalence statement; then read complete Gram-kernel proof.", "original_access_status": "full_text_accessed_partially_inspected", "whole_work_read": false, "record_path": "papers/PAPER-E004.md", "track_file": "papers/equivalence_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": null, "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-E004"]}','On certain Gram matrices and their associated series','["Werner Ehm"]','["C", "F"]','2024',0,0,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','v2','https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.06349v2','3cb69fccea75e07f768e6af5a74ca2ea4640414cbedb9b0875bb5510c8a2d288','papers/PAPER-E004.md','papers/equivalence_records.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('PAPER-E005','corpus/bibliography.jsonl',443,'full_text_accessed','papers/PAPER-E005.md','{"id": "PAPER-E005", "title": "Divided Differences", "authors": ["Carl de Boor"], "date": "2005-02-01", "year": 2005, "doi": null, "arxiv": "math/0502036", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0502036v1", "version": "v1", "family": ["H", "F"], "audit_level": 0, "read_scope": "Partial inspection: §2 continuity; §9 contour Eq51 p63 and Hermite–Genocchi Eq52 pp63–64. Not complete reading or technical audit.", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "venue": "Surveys in Approximation Theory1(2005),46–69", "publication_status": "published_work_preprint_inspected", "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "source_file": "deboor", "reusable_result": "Eq51 represents a divided difference by the contour integral of F over the node polynomial; Eq52 represents it as a simplex integral of the corresponding derivative. Both extend to repeated nodes and supply the exact local grouped-residue identity.", "scope_limit": "Only the stated representation and relevant portions inspected; no full-paper audit.", "source_sha256": "29a84b1a1582225757267de2ad8f96151256e8b35a09ba7907f76cee460c126e", "original_access_status": "full_text_accessed_partially_inspected", "whole_work_read": false, "record_path": "papers/PAPER-E005.md", "track_file": "papers/equivalence_round2_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": null, "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-E005"]}','Divided Differences','["Carl de Boor"]','["H", "F"]','2005',0,0,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','v1','https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0502036v1','29a84b1a1582225757267de2ad8f96151256e8b35a09ba7907f76cee460c126e','papers/PAPER-E005.md','papers/equivalence_round2_records.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('PAPER-E006','corpus/bibliography.jsonl',444,'full_text_accessed','papers/PAPER-E006.md','{"id": "PAPER-E006", "title": "Exponential Riesz bases of subspaces and divided differences", "authors": ["S. A. Avdonin", "S. A. Ivanov"], "date": "2001-03-26", "year": 2001, "doi": null, "arxiv": "math/0103160", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0103160v1", "version": "v1", "family": ["H", "D", "F"], "audit_level": 0, "read_scope": "Partial inspection: Definition1,Eq4,Theorem2 and its proof; Lemma5 and proof pp14–15. No full-paper reading/audit.", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "venue": "arXiv primary preprint version inspected; journal metadata not separately verified", "publication_status": "preprint_version_inspected", "accessed_at": "2026-11-17", "source_file": "avdonin_ivanov", "reusable_result": "Exponential divided differences extend continuously through collisions and remain independent (Theorem2). Lemma5 bounds finite-cluster Gram matrices and inverses uniformly in bounded frequency discs in an upper strip, in L²(0,infinity), using compactness.", "scope_limit": "Our L²(0,1) real-frequency theorem is separately proved; Lemma5 is not quoted as a direct theorem for that different domain. Global Riesz-basis hypotheses are not established for zeta zeros.", "source_sha256": "40a557049e47703b55e670633bc120ac8cc054342fc4f0cac638718c628451b6", "original_access_status": "full_text_accessed_partially_inspected", "whole_work_read": false, "record_path": "papers/PAPER-E006.md", "track_file": "papers/equivalence_round2_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": null, "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-E006"]}','Exponential Riesz bases of subspaces and divided differences','["S. A. Avdonin", "S. A. Ivanov"]','["H", "D", "F"]','2001',0,0,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','v1','https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0103160v1','40a557049e47703b55e670633bc120ac8cc054342fc4f0cac638718c628451b6','papers/PAPER-E006.md','papers/equivalence_round2_records.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('PAPER-SM2017-LOGGROUP','corpus/bibliography.jsonl',445,'full_text_accessed','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md','{"id": "PAPER-SM2017-LOGGROUP", "title": "Hardy inequality and the construction of infinitesimal operators with non-basis family of eigenvectors", "authors": ["Grigory M. Sklyar", "Vitalii Marchenko"], "year": 2017, "date": "2017-02", "preprint_year": 2014, "publication_year": 2017, "venue": "Journal of Functional Analysis 272(3), 1017–1043", "doi": "10.1016/j.jfa.2016.11.001", "arxiv_id": "1405.2731", "canonical_url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfa.2016.11.001", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1405.2731v4", "source_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/sklyar_marchenko_eigenvectors_v4.pdf", "source_sha256": "288b923dc64a851b969d82c5e1db2b9d77db82eb7fa0910b957e3507c6bd3829", "source_bytes": 344804, "version": "arXiv:1405.2731v4; journal identity verified separately", "version_date": "2016-08-24", "current_preprint_version": "v4", "publication_status": "Published journal article. Primary preprints v1–v4 accessed. Publisher version of record inaccessible in this check.", "provider_earlier_date": "2016-11-08", "provider_earlier_date_scope": "OpenAlex publication date and Crossref DOI creation date. Crossref has no separately labeled online-publication date; exact first online publication unverified against publisher text.", "metadata_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/sklyar_marchenko_jfa_crossref.json", "metadata_sha256": "a494ec20022a0dfcf03d49bb12a0619c67f919cc70be925b5d9d76548ec21d9a", "access_date": "2026-11-17", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "full_text_accessed": true, "substantive_reading": true, "whole_work_read": false, "audit_level": 0, "read_scope": "Targeted read of v4 §2.1, Proposition 3 and §3.1 Theorem 6, with v2 §2.1, Proposition 6 and Theorems 8 and 11 read for the exact logarithmic family. Compared v1 Theorem 3.1 and v3 Proposition 6(4) as version witnesses. The full paper and journal proof were not audited.", "correction_history": "v1 Theorem 3.1 prints the additional c_0 condition for the logarithmically multiplied sequence. v2 Theorem 8 replaces it by the maximal difference domain. The universal subsequence clause appears in v2 Proposition 6(4) and remains for infinite subsequences in v3. That proposition and its section were removed in v4. The observation concerns superseded preprints and is not a finding about the journal version.", "manifestations": [{"version": "arXiv v1", "date": "2014-05-12", "posted_at": "2014-05-12T12:40:32Z", "title": "Hardy inequality and the construction of infinitesimal operators with non-Riesz basis family of eigenvectors", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1405.2731v1", "source_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/sklyar_marchenko_eigenvectors_v1.pdf", "source_sha256": "c61381d27ea6593f5b0a0ea03a0fd49ded6e7f32c1e5740f14c34cbe1c2d9845", "scope": "Historical displayed generator domain."}, {"version": "arXiv v2", "date": "2014-09-22", "posted_at": "2014-09-22T12:03:20Z", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1405.2731v2", "source_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/sklyar_marchenko_eigenvectors.pdf", "source_sha256": "70d11b5f0b6b3407c11f4f83ddf3ab56dda7c9e565a8b84214fdd9c04fc537c4", "scope": "Historical Theorem 8, §2.1 and Proposition 6."}, {"version": "arXiv v3", "date": "2014-11-03", "posted_at": "2014-11-03T16:26:56Z", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1405.2731v3", "source_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/sklyar_marchenko_eigenvectors_v3.pdf", "source_sha256": "21daf4b5e2b38ea2fc0d2c56ba73273fd74a07c9eb23d6fd63de21811553edff", "scope": "Historical Proposition 6(4) and Theorem 8 locator."}, {"version": "arXiv v4", "date": "2016-08-24", "posted_at": "2016-08-24T17:15:51Z", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1405.2731v4", "source_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/sklyar_marchenko_eigenvectors_v4.pdf", "source_sha256": "288b923dc64a851b969d82c5e1db2b9d77db82eb7fa0910b957e3507c6bd3829", "scope": "Current preprint, exact operator source and relevant version corrections."}, {"version": "Journal version of record", "date": "2017-02", "source_url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfa.2016.11.001", "access_status": "full_text_inaccessible", "scope": "Crossref identity and issue pagination only."}], "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "selected": true, "family": ["D"], "selection_reason": "Exact antecedent operator family under an explicit unitary difference map, adjoint and time reversal.", "record_path": "papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md", "scope_evidence": ["audits/adversarial_reviews/finite_moment63_manzur_noor_operator_antecedents.md"], "arxiv": "1405.2731", "original_access_status": "full_text_accessed", "track_file": "papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-SM2017-LOGGROUP"]}','Hardy inequality and the construction of infinitesimal operators with non-basis family of eigenvectors','["Grigory M. Sklyar", "Vitalii Marchenko"]','["D"]','2017',0,0,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','arXiv:1405.2731v4; journal identity verified separately','https://arxiv.org/pdf/1405.2731v4','288b923dc64a851b969d82c5e1db2b9d77db82eb7fa0910b957e3507c6bd3829','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('PAPER-SM2021-LOGRESOLVENT','corpus/bibliography.jsonl',446,'full_text_accessed','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md','{"id": "PAPER-SM2021-LOGRESOLVENT", "title": "Resolvent of the generator of the C₀-group with non-basis family of eigenvectors and sharpness of the XYZ theorem", "authors": ["Grigory M. Sklyar", "Vitalii Marchenko"], "year": 2021, "date": "2021-03-12", "publication_year": 2021, "venue": "Journal of Spectral Theory 11(1), 369–386", "doi": "10.4171/JST/344", "arxiv_id": null, "canonical_url": "https://doi.org/10.4171/JST/344", "source_url": "https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/33788", "source_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/sklyar_marchenko_resolvent.pdf", "source_sha256": "682a60a548e39336f93a6a36c4f97d1be2fbfa879b17b5240e25fa619e79fbb7", "source_bytes": 214595, "version": "EMS publisher version of record", "publication_status": "Published journal article; publisher PDF accessed.", "metadata_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/ems_resolution_crossref.json", "metadata_sha256": "97817c5fb8ac66070721bfaa51bc56b32e0d9210a9a56f9548469166d7d36fa4", "access_date": "2026-11-17", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "full_text_accessed": true, "substantive_reading": true, "whole_work_read": false, "audit_level": 0, "read_scope": "Targeted Theorems 1.2, 2.1, and 3.1, including formula (10) and the k=1 resolvent proof. The coefficient resolvent and spectrum apply to the identified logarithmic family. Compactness in the exact model is a deduction from the printed formula. The remainder of the article falls outside this reading.", "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "selected": true, "family": ["D"], "selection_reason": "Direct primary spectrum and resolvent antecedent for the exact logarithmic group, distinct from its original construction paper.", "record_path": "papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md", "scope_evidence": ["audits/adversarial_reviews/finite_moment63_manzur_noor_operator_antecedents.md"], "arxiv": null, "original_access_status": "full_text_accessed", "track_file": "papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-SM2021-LOGRESOLVENT"]}','Resolvent of the generator of the C₀-group with non-basis family of eigenvectors and sharpness of the XYZ theorem','["Grigory M. Sklyar", "Vitalii Marchenko"]','["D"]','2021',0,0,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','EMS publisher version of record','https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/33788','682a60a548e39336f93a6a36c4f97d1be2fbfa879b17b5240e25fa619e79fbb7','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.jsonl');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('PAPER-SMP2021-LINEARGROUP','corpus/bibliography.jsonl',447,'full_text_accessed','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md','{"id": "PAPER-SMP2021-LINEARGROUP", "title": "One Class of Linearly Growing C₀-Groups", "authors": ["Grigory Sklyar", "Vitalii Marchenko", "Piotr Polak"], "year": 2021, "date": "2021", "publication_year": 2021, "reported_published_print_date": "2021-09-25", "reported_published_online_date": "2021-12-25", "publication_date_scope": "Crossref date labels; the primary PDF gives volume and year.", "venue": "Journal of Mathematical Physics, Analysis, Geometry 17(4), 509–520", "doi": "10.15407/mag17.04.509", "arxiv_id": null, "canonical_url": "https://doi.org/10.15407/mag17.04.509", "source_url": "https://jmag.ilt.kharkiv.ua/index.php/jmag/article/download/jm17-0509e/932", "source_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/sklyar_marchenko_polak_linear.pdf", "source_sha256": "7106af34dae09a0e3af4270b1f07a93fd292ff07c7bee93fd8c224d75e9f55de", "source_bytes": 338159, "version": "Journal publisher version of record", "publication_status": "Published journal article; publisher PDF accessed.", "metadata_file": "sources/finite_moment63_operator_antecedents/linear_growth_crossref.json", "metadata_sha256": "9e730cdcada509eee23a86179c4e67aa748b044ded4f239d11680e01cb92a86a", "access_date": "2026-11-17", "access_status": "full_text_accessed", "full_text_accessed": true, "substantive_reading": true, "whole_work_read": false, "audit_level": 0, "read_scope": "Targeted §1 including (1.2) and the explicit logarithmic case, Theorem 2.1, and §4 Theorem 4.2. The checked primary inequalities give two-sided linear growth with constants. They leave the exact pointwise norm formula unspecified. The paper identifies a distinct JFA predecessor for the logarithmic case.", "selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "selected": true, "family": ["D"], "selection_reason": "Direct, accessible primary statement of linear norm growth for the exact operator family, with a distinct title, DOI and three-author byline.", "record_path": "papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md", "scope_evidence": ["audits/adversarial_reviews/finite_moment63_manzur_noor_operator_antecedents.md"], "arxiv": null, "original_access_status": "full_text_accessed", "track_file": "papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.jsonl", "original_selection_status": "selected_checkpoint_priority_work", "source_record_ids": ["PAPER-SMP2021-LINEARGROUP"]}','One Class of Linearly Growing C₀-Groups','["Grigory Sklyar", "Vitalii Marchenko", "Piotr Polak"]','["D"]','2021',0,0,'selected_checkpoint_priority_work','full_text_accessed','Journal publisher version of record','https://jmag.ilt.kharkiv.ua/index.php/jmag/article/download/jm17-0509e/932','7106af34dae09a0e3af4270b1f07a93fd292ff07c7bee93fd8c224d75e9f55de','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.md','papers/finite_moment63_operator_antecedent_records.jsonl');
